<node id="Hooke's Model">
  <data key="d0">Hooke's Model</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Linear-elastic material behavior model applicable when stress is below the proportionality limit&lt;SEP&gt;A specific constitutive model describing linear-elastic material behavior where stress is less than or equal to the proportional limit.&lt;SEP&gt;A material law model describing the elastic behavior of materials under tensile or compressive loading.&lt;SEP&gt;A constitutive law model used in structural analysis, incorporating the modulus of elasticity E to define material behavior.&lt;SEP&gt;Also known as Elastizitätsgesetz, the constitutive law relating stress and strain in the bar element, serving as one of the three fundamental equation types for solving bar problems.&lt;SEP&gt;A constitutive law relating stress and strain in linear-elastic materials.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-424242c0995ba02f22fe1c1864ca5f4b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e6d370949ced2e82caca9443dede62a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a438fa813ee176d3e3d64cd5a7e2dba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e2db8e0cc453f4ff50201dc37d1fa0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f862d3f8b712d95184fc656859d1e6cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-413d03b5c0b6ff01a4da279c609d09f9</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Modulus Of Elasticity">
  <data key="d0">Modulus Of Elasticity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Proportionality factor E in Hooke's model, measured in MPa (N/mm²), representing material stiffness&lt;SEP&gt;A material property measuring the stiffness of an elastic material, covered within the engineering mechanics document.&lt;SEP&gt;A material property measuring stiffness, defined and discussed in the context of the textbook Technische Mechanik 2.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-424242c0995ba02f22fe1c1864ca5f4b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab59a548a45f0f75802088fe89a02c30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3118530638f20d2b532ee5ac5df3f9a0</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stress-Strain Diagram">
  <data key="d0">Stress-Strain Diagram</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Graphical representation of the relationship between stress and strain from tension or compression tests&lt;SEP&gt;Diagram (Spannungs-Dehnungs-Diagramm) constructed using stress and strain data, requiring the stress definition as a prerequisite&lt;SEP&gt;Also known as Spannungs-Dehnungs-Diagramm, a diagram constructed using the strain definition that distinguishes elastic recovery from permanent plastic strain.&lt;SEP&gt;Diagrams resulting from tensile and compressive tests that visually represent the experimentally derived relationship between stress and strain for a material.&lt;SEP&gt;A technical diagram illustrating the mechanical behavior of a ductile material, plotting stress ($\sigma$) against strain ($\varepsilon$) during a tensile test.&lt;SEP&gt;A technical diagram used in materials science and structural mechanics to illustrate the behavior of a material under load.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-424242c0995ba02f22fe1c1864ca5f4b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89b8532cdf159a4bfe5be48dea8b78e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85da86ad0233986cf40614b65dc61ad2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-763b254f857bc066044052010175b2b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-055d89277cf2e87034384489ad8dc567&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73a8a17ee36ec3a25041cb22c3b85cd5</data>
