</node>
<node id="Hooke's Law">
  <data key="d0">Hooke's Law</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Hooke's Law is a fundamental principle of physics and linear elasticity that describes the relationship between stress and strain in elastic materials. Often referred to as a constitutive law or material model (such as the German terms "Hooksches Modell" or "Elastizitätsgesetz"), it establishes a linear relationship where normal stress is directly proportional to strain via a proportionality constant known as Young's modulus or the elastic modulus (E). This relationship is mathematically expressed as sigma = E * epsilon, or inversely as epsilon = sigma / E. Hooke's Law applies strictly within the linear-elastic regime—specifically the initial elastic region of the stress-strain diagram where stress does not exceed the proportional limit—and relies on the assumption of small deformations for its linearization. Beyond standard mechanical applications, the principle is also extended to model thermoelasticity.

In engineering and structural mechanics, Hooke's Law connects the normal stress equation to kinematic relationships to analyze elastic deformation behavior. For slender structural members and prismatic bars under uniaxial tension and compression, the principle is used to derive mechanical strain components and calculate axial deformation. It relates the change in length of a bar to the internal axial force, initial length, and axial rigidity (EA), expressed by the physical law delta L = FL / EA or delta l = Sl / EA. This fundamental equation is essential for computing the mechanical elongation or elastic shortening of rod segments based on material properties and internal forces.

As a foundational constitutive model, Hooke's Law serves as a critical component in solving complex structural problems, including statically indeterminate systems. When integrated with equilibrium and kinematic compatibility conditions, it allows engineers to relate bar forces to elongations and ultimately determine axial force distributions, stresses, and displacements. Combining this elasticity law with other fundamental mechanics equations produces the governing ordinary differential equation for displacement. This makes Hooke's Law a vital framework extensively covered in engineering education and technical literature, such as the textbook "Technische Mechanik 2".&lt;SEP&gt;A physical law used for elastic deformation calculations in the context of stress analysis</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6fc1a89775e67ed1be0c24a11e1773f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe61c354100bb43a98ebc62d57cf28c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-738c698a563cc3405e3c1de5794fa318&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf7cfa532d0224ec6532c6354495df59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc78afbb216db05f32ee167a8643581f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad1fe24f4724db937ef65aa2cd2c2fab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61bee0456fb356f553c6809b0f9fb7ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f197243eeecfe8da4e162edc85af353&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9650cbfdac35d71c763ff0baacdc1c9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cc011b4f71d9c304cbdecd2839b81e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23f9a8f34af690fb6d5cb0ea12f409a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d49057dad0c3acc1a3ce1afb3e687a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4f759f99f5a784630c625df026ca993&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe1aa2ab22c57b58f370cf064cf7ce98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f72457639c5767731980d0c54a4fe069&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edab2d4bca40b7e16cfc072b04cebe0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89b8532cdf159a4bfe5be48dea8b78e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76cd2fb9e592523746e131ec4c914481&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85da86ad0233986cf40614b65dc61ad2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9966746921724686a393e234327d9e41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6e4242a538dfbd7e7ae0462ee78fbc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-763b254f857bc066044052010175b2b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ad3e7d061ebaf26776716772bd7daeb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-055d89277cf2e87034384489ad8dc567&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-783555881f4ab73d4d04ea548b9fae1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fed5dfab36680bc0a576b0ed9cc7e5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-151ad67dcab298d7226da28fe7afb340&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42f0665902c9df9b5ec4573eb02f74a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e6d370949ced2e82caca9443dede62a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a7f9fd51bacb1b5261081565de649fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ab72d2dd30449c995d80393a0354227&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abc3cadf3a789dbb882aa778366ab3b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-677c3b37a16b17c8907603bf39babaae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73a8a17ee36ec3a25041cb22c3b85cd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab59a548a45f0f75802088fe89a02c30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3118530638f20d2b532ee5ac5df3f9a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c71f393772a794391e49730d47a8bda4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-faaf238bf3e3a6116edca46159e939df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-635877c2ca4bd8652a8de3e6ef23d5f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-794d30f8b956a266f2b6d66cc7f678de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b12d2d988ba8fdb94bda0bb9243511d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd290e24d36ba227108f0e9b5c1965e</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
