<node id="Bar 2">
  <data key="d0">Bar 2</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Bar 2 refers to distinct structural members depending on whether it is analyzed within a two-bar structural system or a three-bar structural system.

In the context of a statically determinate two-bar truss system, Bar 2 is an inclined structural member that extends downwards from Point B, terminating at Joint C. Oriented at an angle α, this inclined bar operates under tension and bears a force calculated as S₂ = F/(sin(α)cos(α)). 

Alternatively, within a statically indeterminate three-bar structural system, Bar 2 functions as the central vertical structural element. It is suspended along the centerline from a fixed support, pinned at its upper end to the ceiling, and attached at its lower end to node K. The bar is characterized by a specific length denoted as l and an axial rigidity (or stiffness) of EA₂. Its mechanical behavior dictates that its elongation (Δl₂) equals the vertical displacement of node K and is mathematically related to the elongation of Bar 1 through a structural compatibility equation. In this three-bar configuration, Bar 2 carries an internal axial force S₂, and in the limiting case where the angle α approaches 90°, this vertical bar is structured to carry the entire applied load.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fe61c354100bb43a98ebc62d57cf28c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed3c14262e18f66ed415c1b72900af48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b9805139d42f6eef23df04f62f07811&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad1fe24f4724db937ef65aa2cd2c2fab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e7848db5af896e14553322ef7578977&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d49057dad0c3acc1a3ce1afb3e687a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f72457639c5767731980d0c54a4fe069&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1db4055b5d566c7d454787a7ff1515b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76cd2fb9e592523746e131ec4c914481&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9966746921724686a393e234327d9e41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94aa1e1d6b738ff40ac94957c9a7084a</data>
