<node id="Thermal Loading">
  <data key="d0">Thermal Loading</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Thermal effects denoted by ΔT≠0 that require thermal strain terms to be incorporated into the structural calculations&lt;SEP&gt;The application of a temperature change to a structural member, resulting in thermal expansion or contraction and associated internal stresses.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of loading involving temperature changes (ΔT), featured in a statically indeterminate rod example on page 15.&lt;SEP&gt;The thermal condition applied to the bar, represented by a uniform temperature change.&lt;SEP&gt;The thermal load applied to section 1 of the statically indeterminate bar, causing constrained thermal expansion.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of loading involving temperature changes that induces thermal stresses in structural systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The application of thermal effects to a structure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-738c698a563cc3405e3c1de5794fa318&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0963d089a81497869e206f806e6e66d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd50f7cb97e77515d873719c81dafca9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccf2b44f3719aa488a2e1148c9ed36db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a93c57c2e2028051403eda908d55fe3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06a907de5d496ddcf9ab58b307c8f8ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e6428916bed03d77d29954942400a6f</data>
