<node id="Small Deformations">
  <data key="d0">Small Deformations</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A theoretical restriction where the absolute value of epsilon is much less than 1, necessary for linearizing subsequent mechanical equations.&lt;SEP&gt;An assumption required for the validity of the superposition principle, implying that geometric changes due to deformation are negligible.&lt;SEP&gt;An assumption in displacement analysis where circular arcs can be approximated by tangents.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-71dad38576055c6e013578d06064a913&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f197243eeecfe8da4e162edc85af353&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9650cbfdac35d71c763ff0baacdc1c9c</data>
