<node id="Kinematic Relationship">
  <data key="d0">Kinematic Relationship</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A relationship within section 10.4 connecting thermal effects to deformation in structural analysis, of which the thermal expansion law forms a part</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a371746d42ee15c97ccf2f983b9237ee</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896969</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Kinematic Compatibility">
  <data key="d0">Kinematic Compatibility</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Conditions (Kinematik) ensuring deformations are geometrically consistent in a structure, required for analyzing statically indeterminate systems&lt;SEP&gt;A physical condition stating that the displacements of the structural bars must conform to the system's geometry.&lt;SEP&gt;The geometric compatibility condition relating bar elongations, specifically Δl1 = Δl2 cos α, contributing two cos α factors to the equation through Hooke's law.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a371746d42ee15c97ccf2f983b9237ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edab2d4bca40b7e16cfc072b04cebe0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76cd2fb9e592523746e131ec4c914481</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896969</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Elastic Constitutive Law">
  <data key="d0">Elastic Constitutive Law</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The material law (Elasitzitätsgesetz) relating stress and strain in elastic deformation, characterized by extensional stiffness EA</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a371746d42ee15c97ccf2f983b9237ee</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896969</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Extensional Stiffness">
  <data key="d0">Extensional Stiffness</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Denoted as EA, a measure of resistance to axial deformation in a structural member, part of the elastic constitutive law&lt;SEP&gt;The axial stiffnesses (Dehnsteifigkeiten) of the bars, where the stiffness of bar 3 equals that of bar 1.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a371746d42ee15c97ccf2f983b9237ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edab2d4bca40b7e16cfc072b04cebe0c</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896969</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mechanical Strain">
  <data key="d0">Mechanical Strain</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The elastic mechanical strain component, calculated as normal stress divided by Young's modulus.&lt;SEP&gt;The component of strain caused by axial loading, calculated as the internal normal force divided by tensile stiffness.&lt;SEP&gt;The component of total strain, calculated as N/EA, caused by internal normal force.&lt;SEP&gt;Denoted as ε, the strain due to mechanical loading, defined as σ/E = N/(EA)&lt;SEP&gt;Derivative of displacement u' = ε with respect to position x, representing the mechanical deformation of the bar.&lt;SEP&gt;The strain component N/(EA) derived from Hooke's Law, representing deformation due to mechanical loading through the internal normal force and axial rigidity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a371746d42ee15c97ccf2f983b9237ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c97b092fc202625d8ee8acd1894cf787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f197243eeecfe8da4e162edc85af353&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fb28b0e78717850205497e7c5e164dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-794d30f8b956a266f2b6d66cc7f678de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7f547ed992922c6608475aa607ecc95</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896969</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Statically Determinate System">
  <data key="d0">Statically Determinate System</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A structural system where thermal expansion produces deformation without inducing additional normal forces or stresses, as the structure can freely deform&lt;SEP&gt;A structural system where the phenomenon of internal forces arising from thermal loading without external mechanical loads is absent.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a371746d42ee15c97ccf2f983b9237ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c71f393772a794391e49730d47a8bda4</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896969</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Statically Indeterminate System">
  <data key="d0">Statically Indeterminate System</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A structural system where constrained thermal expansion generates internal forces and additional stresses beyond mechanical loading&lt;SEP&gt;A system where support reactions cannot be determined by static equilibrium alone, described in the surrounding text.&lt;SEP&gt;A structural system where support reactions cannot be determined by static equilibrium alone; in this case, a compound rod with both ends fixed (beidseitig eingespannt)&lt;SEP&gt;A structural system where internal forces arise from thermal loading even without external mechanical loads.&lt;SEP&gt;A structural system that cannot be solved by equilibrium equations alone and requires additional compatibility conditions</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a371746d42ee15c97ccf2f983b9237ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe1aa2ab22c57b58f370cf064cf7ce98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccf2b44f3719aa488a2e1148c9ed36db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ab72d2dd30449c995d80393a0354227&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c71f393772a794391e49730d47a8bda4</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896969</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Total Deformation">
  <data key="d0">Total Deformation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The combined deformation resulting from the superposition of thermal strain and mechanical strain, integrated as u = ∫ ε dx for variable cross-sections&lt;SEP&gt;A physical observable representing the overall change in shape or size of a structural member under loading.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a371746d42ee15c97ccf2f983b9237ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0963d089a81497869e206f806e6e66d1</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896969</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Civil Engineering">
  <data key="d0">Civil Engineering</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A field of engineering where the thermal expansion law is essential for analyzing thermal stresses in constrained structures and bridge design&lt;SEP&gt;A field of engineering in which the equilibrium equation is essential for analyzing axially loaded members such as columns, cables, bars, and rods.&lt;SEP&gt;An engineering field where stress transformation is used extensively for stress analysis of loaded components</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a371746d42ee15c97ccf2f983b9237ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cc011b4f71d9c304cbdecd2839b81e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3780797c1d45f39538f2b68c98e007f0</data>
