  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The angle formed between horizontal bar 1 and inclined bar 2 at joint C.&lt;SEP&gt;An angle defining the orientation of force S_2, indicated by a curved arc between the horizontal line of force S_1 and the vector of force S_2&lt;SEP&gt;The geometric angle denoted by the Greek letter alpha, located between Bar 1 and Bar 2 at Joint C.&lt;SEP&gt;The angle between Bar 1 and Bar 2 in the three-bar system, whose cosine appears in the compatibility equation relating their elongations.&lt;SEP&gt;The angle denoted by the Greek letter alpha, representing the inclination of Bar 1 and Bar 3 relative to the vertical axis.&lt;SEP&gt;The angle formed by Bar Force S1 and Bar Force S3 relative to Bar Force S2.</data>
