</node>
<node id="x">
  <data key="d0">x</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The axial coordinate measured from the smaller-radius end [m], which serves as a normalized coordinate parameter.&lt;SEP&gt;A variable labeled in the diagram indicating the distance from the left origin to the left boundary of the green differential segment in the undeformed bar.&lt;SEP&gt;The longitudinal coordinate along the one-dimensional structural element.&lt;SEP&gt;The position along the rod measured from the fixed support at the top, with x = 0 at the fixed end and x = l at the free end.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1b5a4dfb0ae1aefebcb3a9f19f155c76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cc011b4f71d9c304cbdecd2839b81e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba3dc6bb30208edf4354dd20376fa9f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-213cdd3f8f32396583dc5a4fa4d54dfd</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896973</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="A(x)">
  <data key="d0">A(x)</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The cross-sectional area of the circular cross-section at axial position x, computed as π·r(x)².</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1b5a4dfb0ae1aefebcb3a9f19f155c76</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896973</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="σ(x)">
  <data key="d0">σ(x)</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The normal stress distribution calculated as N(x)/A(x), representing a position-dependent stress field.&lt;SEP&gt;The axial stress (normal stress) at position x along the hanging rod, varying linearly from G/A at the fixed end to zero at the free end.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1b5a4dfb0ae1aefebcb3a9f19f155c76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-213cdd3f8f32396583dc5a4fa4d54dfd</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896973</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="N(x)">
  <data key="d0">N(x)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The constant compressive internal force within the bar, equal to -F.&lt;SEP&gt;The internal normal force (Normalkraft) as a function of the longitudinal coordinate, representing the axial force within the structural element.&lt;SEP&gt;The internal normal force at position x, decreasing linearly from G at the support to zero at the free end as only the rod's weight below section x contributes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1b5a4dfb0ae1aefebcb3a9f19f155c76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cc011b4f71d9c304cbdecd2839b81e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-213cdd3f8f32396583dc5a4fa4d54dfd</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896973</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Truncated Cone Geometry">
  <data key="d0">Truncated Cone Geometry</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The geometric shape of the conical bar, characterized by a linear variation in radius and a constant taper angle.</data>
