  <data key="d0">Equation</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A mathematical equation representing the vertical displacement of Node K in a statically indeterminate three-bar structural system.&lt;SEP&gt;Mathematical formula that calculates the axial forces S₁ and S₃ in a statically indeterminate three-bar truss system, derived by simultaneously solving equilibrium conditions, Hooke's Law, and kinematic compatibility conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;A mathematical equation presented in LaTeX format that appears nonsensical, likely the result of a severe Optical Character Recognition (OCR) error or parsing artifact.&lt;SEP&gt;The mathematical equation $a(0,0) = \frac{11}{12} \times (0,0)$ representing an evaluation of a coefficient function at the origin, involving scalar multiplication of the zero vector by a rational coefficient, which reduces to the trivial identity $a(0,0) = (0,0)$.&lt;SEP&gt;A computational example or derivation step written in LaTeX format, containing numerical values, the factor of 2, and a circled marker ①.</data>
