<node id="Constitutive Law">
  <data key="d0">Constitutive Law</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The third of three fundamental equation types for bar problems, describing material behavior such as Hooke's model (Elastizitätsgesetz).&lt;SEP&gt;Also known as Stoffgesetz, it is one of the three governing equation types required to solve for stresses and deformations in statically indeterminate systems.&lt;SEP&gt;One of three fundamental equation types needed to determine stresses and deformations in a bar, represented by Hooke's law relating material stress and strain behavior&lt;SEP&gt;Fundamental principle of structural mechanics relating stress and strain, specifically incorporating elasticity and thermal effects in this context.&lt;SEP&gt;The physical relationship between applied forces and material deformation.&lt;SEP&gt;The stress-strain relationship governing material behavior in the system, instantiated by Hooke's law in this context.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ad1fe24f4724db937ef65aa2cd2c2fab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c97b092fc202625d8ee8acd1894cf787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76cd2fb9e592523746e131ec4c914481&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-413d03b5c0b6ff01a4da279c609d09f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-faaf238bf3e3a6116edca46159e939df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fb28b0e78717850205497e7c5e164dc</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896991</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
