<node id="Technical Engineering Diagram">
  <data key="d0">Technical Engineering Diagram</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">This technical engineering diagram illustrates the distribution of normal stress in a straight bar subjected to axial tensile forces.&lt;SEP&gt;The visual representation illustrating the statically determinate two-bar truss system.&lt;SEP&gt;An image illustrating a two-dimensional stress state on a material element, characterized by clean vector lines and high-contrast colors typical of academic textbooks.&lt;SEP&gt;A technical engineering diagram illustrating the stress state within a thin-walled cylindrical pressure vessel (Dünnwandiger Kessel), divided into four distinct panels labeled a, b, c, and d, using grey shading for solid vessel components, bright red for vector quantities such as pressure and stress, and black typography for mathematical symbols and dimensions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8f7107d9e481e8d7b78079a1c4ff9229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94aa1e1d6b738ff40ac94957c9a7084a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98f7f241f746726b97e3dc567365e483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b026fcfc3bb4dcf15d90b692b7902eb</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904035</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diagram A">
  <data key="d0">Diagram A</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">This figure serves as the primary reference model depicting a gray rectangular bar with a longitudinal axis and specific cross-sectional planes.&lt;SEP&gt;A technical schematic diagram illustrating a horizontal bar fixed at both ends, composed of two distinct segments.&lt;SEP&gt;A schematic diagram displaying a horizontal bar composed of two segments attached to rigid supports B and C.&lt;SEP&gt;A three-dimensional isometric view of a grey cylindrical pressure vessel showing its diameter (2r), internal pressure (p), and a highlighted green square element on the outer surface.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8f7107d9e481e8d7b78079a1c4ff9229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccf2b44f3719aa488a2e1148c9ed36db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df979c16e8c52bf800fb84c3a4a4bdea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-887f545fd528c5ed1b7980ed83618c38</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903832</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diagram B">
  <data key="d0">Diagram B</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">This figure focuses on the region near cut 's-s' and shows the non-uniform stress distribution at the points where external forces are applied.&lt;SEP&gt;A simplified mechanical model or free-body diagram of the horizontal bar showing reaction forces.&lt;SEP&gt;A free-body-style representation of the two-segment bar showing compressive reaction forces at positions B and C.&lt;SEP&gt;A technical diagram illustrating the free-body diagram of a central node designated as K.&lt;SEP&gt;A magnified two-dimensional view of the green square element from the vessel surface, showing tensile stresses on all four faces with horizontal arrows labeled σ_x and vertical arrows labeled σ_φ.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8f7107d9e481e8d7b78079a1c4ff9229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdfa6405eb28772fd593fe970821beaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccf2b44f3719aa488a2e1148c9ed36db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df979c16e8c52bf800fb84c3a4a4bdea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-887f545fd528c5ed1b7980ed83618c38</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903832</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diagram C">
  <data key="d0">Diagram C</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">This figure corresponds to the cut 's'-s'' at the notch and depicts a pronounced outward curve or 'bulge' indicating stress concentration.&lt;SEP&gt;A technical diagram presenting the Verschiebungsplan, which details the kinematic compatibility of the structural system.&lt;SEP&gt;A three-dimensional perspective technical schematic diagram showing a cylindrical pressure vessel with wall thickness 't', used to analyze force equilibrium in the longitudinal (x) direction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8f7107d9e481e8d7b78079a1c4ff9229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdfa6405eb28772fd593fe970821beaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-290ff749460960cc500499bfce8172f5</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
