</node>
<node id="Hängender Stab Unter Eigengewicht">
  <data key="d0">Hängender Stab Unter Eigengewicht</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An example problem of a hanging bar under self-weight with statically determinate conditions, constant cross-sectional area, constant axial stiffness, and constant temperature change, used to determine length change and stress.&lt;SEP&gt;A statically determinate problem in elastostatics involving a hanging bar subjected to its own weight.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cc79c4ab764f023bc17eed0dd0b44b48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17b87724a453e2805522671a76c088ec</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Axial Stiffness E·A">
  <data key="d0">Axial Stiffness E·A</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A material and structural property of the hanging bar that is constant (E·A = const.) under the given conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cc79c4ab764f023bc17eed0dd0b44b48</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Temperature Change ΔT">
  <data key="d0">Temperature Change ΔT</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A loading condition applied to the hanging bar problem that is constant (ΔT = const.) under the given conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;The constant temperature difference denoted by ΔT, relevant to thermal loading in the governing differential equation for statically indeterminate structures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cc79c4ab764f023bc17eed0dd0b44b48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0963d089a81497869e206f806e6e66d1</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Length Change Δl">
  <data key="d0">Length Change Δl</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A deformation result determined in the hanging bar problem, representing the change in length of the bar.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cc79c4ab764f023bc17eed0dd0b44b48</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stress σ">
  <data key="d0">Stress σ</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A mechanical quantity determined in the hanging bar problem, representing the internal stress distribution in the bar.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cc79c4ab764f023bc17eed0dd0b44b48</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
