  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Boundary Condition U(x=0) = 0">
  <data key="d0">Boundary Condition U(x=0) = 0</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A condition in the hanging bar problem specifying that the displacement at x=0 is zero, which results in the integration constant C₂ being zero.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cc79c4ab764f023bc17eed0dd0b44b48</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Boundary Condition U'(x=l) = 0">
  <data key="d0">Boundary Condition U'(x=l) = 0</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A condition in the hanging bar problem specifying that the derivative of displacement at x=l is zero, which results in the integration constant C₁ being equal to G.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cc79c4ab764f023bc17eed0dd0b44b48</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Integration Constant C₂">
  <data key="d0">Integration Constant C₂</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A constant of integration determined to be zero based on the boundary condition u(x=0) = 0.&lt;SEP&gt;A constant of integration derived from the fixed support boundary condition at x=0, equal to 0.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cc79c4ab764f023bc17eed0dd0b44b48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-460d07ec9180c3a338bcc5988e8e42a2</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Integration Constant C₁">
  <data key="d0">Integration Constant C₁</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A constant of integration determined to be equal to G based on the boundary condition u′(x=l) = 0.&lt;SEP&gt;A constant of integration derived from the stress-free boundary condition at the free end, equal to G/EA.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cc79c4ab764f023bc17eed0dd0b44b48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-460d07ec9180c3a338bcc5988e8e42a2</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Statically Determinate Conditions">
  <data key="d0">Statically Determinate Conditions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A structural condition characterizing the hanging bar problem, indicating that the reaction forces can be determined purely from equations of static equilibrium.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cc79c4ab764f023bc17eed0dd0b44b48</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Undeformed Bar">
  <data key="d0">Undeformed Bar</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Represented as a solid grey horizontal rectangle, it illustrates a bar in its original state before deformation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba3dc6bb30208edf4354dd20376fa9f6</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deformed Bar">
  <data key="d0">Deformed Bar</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Represented as a solid grey horizontal rectangle, it illustrates a bar after deformation, appearing slightly elongated or shifted relative to the undeformed bar.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba3dc6bb30208edf4354dd20376fa9f6</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Differential Segment">
  <data key="d0">Differential Segment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A small highlighted segment within the bar used to analyze the change in length and local strain.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba3dc6bb30208edf4354dd20376fa9f6</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Local Strain">
  <data key="d0">Local Strain</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Also known as technical strain or Dehnung, it is defined as the change in length divided by the original length of the differential segment.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of strain defined specifically in the context of structural components such as bars with varying cross-sections.&lt;SEP&gt;Denoted by ε(x) = du(x)/dx, the local formulation of strain as the first spatial derivative of the displacement function, extending the global strain definition to a position-dependent context.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba3dc6bb30208edf4354dd20376fa9f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40c9b6d63b8c22a4bba35a9a76979235&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85da86ad0233986cf40614b65dc61ad2</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="dx">
  <data key="d0">dx</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A variable labeled with green double-headed arrows representing the width of the initial differential segment in the undeformed bar, also referred to as the original length.&lt;SEP&gt;The geometric dimension labeled in green text representing the length of the horizontal leg along the x-axis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba3dc6bb30208edf4354dd20376fa9f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c2cf3a337f73c88af5880c2708e9c48</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904052</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="u">
  <data key="d0">u</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A variable labeled in green representing the displacement of the left boundary of the differential segment, which has moved to the right by this distance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba3dc6bb30208edf4354dd20376fa9f6</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="u+du">
  <data key="d0">u+du</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A variable labeled in green representing the total displacement of the right boundary of the differential segment in the deformed bar.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba3dc6bb30208edf4354dd20376fa9f6</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="dx+(u+du)-u">
  <data key="d0">dx+(u+du)-u</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A mathematical expression in green text shown below the deformed bar representing the calculation for the new, deformed length of the differential element.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba3dc6bb30208edf4354dd20376fa9f6</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Compatibility Equation">
  <data key="d0">Compatibility Equation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The equation Δl₁ = Δl₂ cos α representing a kinematic compatibility condition for a statically indeterminate three-bar system, stating that the elongation of bar 1 equals the elongation of bar 2 multiplied by the cosine of angle α between them.&lt;SEP&gt;An equation accounting for structural constraints, into which the elastic lengthening and geometric factors are substituted during the derivation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f72457639c5767731980d0c54a4fe069&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9966746921724686a393e234327d9e41</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Three-bar System">
  <data key="d0">Three-bar System</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A statically indeterminate structural system consisting of three bars connected at a common node K, subjected to an external force F.&lt;SEP&gt;A statically indeterminate structural system consisting of one vertical bar (bar 2) and two inclined bars (bars 1 and 3), also referred to as "einfach statisch unbestimmt gelagertes Stabsystem."</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f72457639c5767731980d0c54a4fe069&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76cd2fb9e592523746e131ec4c914481</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Small Displacements">
  <data key="d0">Small Displacements</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An assumption in the geometric analysis where circular arcs can be approximated by their tangents, used to derive the elongation of the inclined bar.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f72457639c5767731980d0c54a4fe069</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bar Forces">
  <data key="d0">Bar Forces</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The internal forces S₁, S₂, and S₃ within the bars of the three-bar system, which are determined by combining compatibility, constitutive, and equilibrium equations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f72457639c5767731980d0c54a4fe069</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
