  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Δl">
  <data key="d0">Δl</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A variable representing the elongation of the bar caused by its weight.&lt;SEP&gt;The total thermal elongation of the bar, resulting from integrating the linear thermal strain ε_T over the bar length&lt;SEP&gt;Change in length, denoted as Längenänderung, of the bar or rod element</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-17b87724a453e2805522671a76c088ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-370a72fe18982a27d4543ffa0c4c20f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-542bf3a4290d267cd5257b52563c594f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="σ">
  <data key="d0">σ</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A variable representing the normal stress within the bar caused by its weight.&lt;SEP&gt;The Greek letter sigma representing normal stress, labeled on the horizontal axis of the coordinate system used in Mohr's Circle.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-17b87724a453e2805522671a76c088ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-842c0517bb20a54922d1a75c277c68f0</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903867</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Strain-Displacement Equation">
  <data key="d0">Strain-Displacement Equation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The equation ε(x) = du/dx = Δl/l representing the fundamental strain-displacement relationship in one-dimensional continuum mechanics, establishing the local strain field as the spatial derivative of the displacement field</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5ae0372192096a8671eab765c6a11a90</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Engineering Strain">
  <data key="d0">Engineering Strain</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The dimensionless ratio of total elongation Δl to original length l, also called technical strain, applicable for homogeneous deformation&lt;SEP&gt;Also known as Technische Dehnung, the fundamental definition of strain in one-dimensional continuum mechanics, defined as the ratio of change in length to original reference length, denoted by ε. It is a dimensionless kinematic quantity describing the geometry of deformation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5ae0372192096a8671eab765c6a11a90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85da86ad0233986cf40614b65dc61ad2</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Small Deformation Hypothesis">
  <data key="d0">Small Deformation Hypothesis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The assumption that |Δl| ≪ l or |ε| ≪ 1, which linearizes the strain measure in the kinematic description of deformation</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5ae0372192096a8671eab765c6a11a90</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stress-Strain Diagrams">
  <data key="d0">Stress-Strain Diagrams</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Graphical representations discussed in subsequent pages that relate stress to strain, building upon the foundation of kinematic measures.&lt;SEP&gt;Diagrams used for analyzing elastic bodies under load through tensile/compressive testing&lt;SEP&gt;Diagrams visualizing the results of tensile and compression tests.&lt;SEP&gt;Graphical representations of stress-strain relationships mentioned in the text.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5ae0372192096a8671eab765c6a11a90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40c9b6d63b8c22a4bba35a9a76979235&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7191762e3c837260ad5bf3f1bc50f25a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b35bef5073db0c5a31b6dd2e83c0ddb</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Kinematic Description Of Deformation">
  <data key="d0">Kinematic Description Of Deformation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The geometric foundation necessary for formulating constitutive laws, describing the deformation kinematics of elastic bodies</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5ae0372192096a8671eab765c6a11a90</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Total Elongation">
  <data key="d0">Total Elongation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Denoted as Δl, representing the total change in length of the bar, where positive values indicate elongation and negative values indicate compression.&lt;SEP&gt;The overall change in length of a structural member, calculated as the integral of the longitudinal strain field over the member's length.&lt;SEP&gt;The global deformation of the rod, denoted as Delta l, calculated as the difference in displacements at the endpoints.&lt;SEP&gt;The total change in length of a member, set to zero in geometric compatibility equations for statically indeterminate structures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5ae0372192096a8671eab765c6a11a90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-920d899bb09d20ddc75b79ec193db2e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-635877c2ca4bd8652a8de3e6ef23d5f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7f547ed992922c6608475aa607ecc95</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tensile/Compressive Testing">
  <data key="d0">Tensile/Compressive Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A testing method used to analyze elastic bodies under load, often in conjunction with stress-strain diagrams.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5ae0372192096a8671eab765c6a11a90</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Elastic Bodies">
  <data key="d0">Elastic Bodies</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Physical objects analyzed under load, whose behavior is ultimately understood through the strain-displacement relationship and constitutive laws.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5ae0372192096a8671eab765c6a11a90</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="First-Order Ordinary Differential Equation">
  <data key="d0">First-Order Ordinary Differential Equation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The mathematical classification of the strain-displacement equation, which relates the displacement field to the strain field and allows integration to recover displacements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5ae0372192096a8671eab765c6a11a90</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stabsysteme">
  <data key="d0">Stabsysteme</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bar systems analyzed as statically determinate and indeterminate within the field of engineering mechanics, discussed in the surrounding document and covered by Technische Mechanik 2.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f3cdf7e6c0e0814f6340adcf0330c36f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Elasticity">
  <data key="d0">Elasticity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A mechanical property discussed in the context of the Hookesches Modell.&lt;SEP&gt;A property of materials and a topic in mechanics discussed in the surrounding document and covered by Technische Mechanik 2.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f3cdf7e6c0e0814f6340adcf0330c36f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b35bef5073db0c5a31b6dd2e83c0ddb</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Advanced Engineering Mechanics">
  <data key="d0">Advanced Engineering Mechanics</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A broader field of engineering discussed in the surrounding document, encompassing the analysis of bar systems, kinematics, and elasticity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f3cdf7e6c0e0814f6340adcf0330c36f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Displacement Diagrams">
  <data key="d0">Displacement Diagrams</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Technical diagrams presented on the slides that are used to visually represent and validate concepts within the educational lecture.</data>
