<node id="Bar Element">
  <data key="d0">Bar Element</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Also known as Stabelement, a structural member or physical object whose absolute change in length is evaluated when subjected to mechanical loading.&lt;SEP&gt;A one-dimensional structural element (Einzelstab) under axial loading in structural mechanics, analyzed using infinitesimal elements to derive the equilibrium condition.&lt;SEP&gt;A single structural element (Einzelstab) subjected to point forces and distributed line loads, used in trusses, columns, and other load-bearing components in structural mechanics&lt;SEP&gt;A rod or physical element whose thermal expansion and change in length are described by the equation</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-85da86ad0233986cf40614b65dc61ad2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-370a72fe18982a27d4543ffa0c4c20f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-413d03b5c0b6ff01a4da279c609d09f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-faaf238bf3e3a6116edca46159e939df</data>
