</node>
<node id="Geometric Length Relation">
  <data key="d0">Geometric Length Relation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A geometric constraint combined with kinematics that contributes to the numerator's cos² α term by projecting node K's displacement onto the inclined bars.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9966746921724686a393e234327d9e41</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="N(x) Equation">
  <data key="d0">N(x) Equation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mathematical equation N(x) = EA·u'(x) = G(1 - x/l) representing the axial force distribution in a vertically hanging rod under self-weight, combining Hooke's constitutive relation with the equilibrium solution derived from the governing differential equation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a6e4242a538dfbd7e7ae0462ee78fbc7</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Axial Force Distribution">
  <data key="d0">Axial Force Distribution</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The internal axial force N(x) at position x along the rod, exhibiting a linear distribution from maximum value G at the top support to zero at the free end.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a6e4242a538dfbd7e7ae0462ee78fbc7</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vertically Hanging Rod Under Self-Weight">
  <data key="d0">Vertically Hanging Rod Under Self-Weight</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A structural system consisting of a rod hanging vertically subjected to its own weight, classified as statically determinate, where support reactions are determined from equilibrium alone.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a6e4242a538dfbd7e7ae0462ee78fbc7</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
