  <data key="d3">chunk-bbd27ba75933ee3cba54b55605c1c8dc</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infinitesimal Rod Element">
  <data key="d0">Infinitesimal Rod Element</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A differential element of length dx along the longitudinal axis of a bar, used to isolate a differential segment of a one-dimensional load-bearing member for deriving governing differential equations in continuum mechanics and structural analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e2db8e0cc453f4ff50201dc37d1fa0c</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bar (Stab)">
  <data key="d0">Bar (Stab)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A one-dimensional load-bearing member along whose longitudinal axis the infinitesimal rod element is defined.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e2db8e0cc453f4ff50201dc37d1fa0c</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Distributed Load n(x)">
  <data key="d0">Distributed Load n(x)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Distributed loads acting along a rod element, related to internal normal force through the equilibrium condition.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e2db8e0cc453f4ff50201dc37d1fa0c</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Modulus Of Elasticity E">
  <data key="d0">Modulus Of Elasticity E</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A material property parameter used in Hooke's model for formulating the constitutive law.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e2db8e0cc453f4ff50201dc37d1fa0c</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Equilibrium Condition (Gleichgewichtsbedingung)">
  <data key="d0">Equilibrium Condition (Gleichgewichtsbedingung)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">One of three foundational equation types in single rod analysis, relating internal normal force N(x) to distributed loads n(x).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e2db8e0cc453f4ff50201dc37d1fa0c</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Differential Equation dN/dx + n = 0">
  <data key="d0">Differential Equation dN/dx + n = 0</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The governing differential equation for axial force distribution, formulated using the infinitesimal element approach.&lt;SEP&gt;A mathematical equation representing the differential equilibrium condition for a one-dimensional bar element under axial loading. It states that the spatial derivative of the internal normal force N(x) along the bar's longitudinal axis x plus the distributed line load n per unit length must equal zero for static equilibrium.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e2db8e0cc453f4ff50201dc37d1fa0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-413d03b5c0b6ff01a4da279c609d09f9</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Free-Body Diagrams">
  <data key="d0">Free-Body Diagrams</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Discrete analytical technique from which the infinitesimal element approach enables the transition to continuous field equations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e2db8e0cc453f4ff50201dc37d1fa0c</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thermal Effects (ΔT)">
  <data key="d0">Thermal Effects (ΔT)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of loading condition, alongside mechanical forces, affecting a rod's deformation behavior.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e2db8e0cc453f4ff50201dc37d1fa0c</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mechanical Forces">
  <data key="d0">Mechanical Forces</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of loading condition, alongside thermal effects (ΔT), affecting a rod's deformation behavior under various loading scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e2db8e0cc453f4ff50201dc37d1fa0c</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Continuous Field Equations">
  <data key="d0">Continuous Field Equations</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Mathematical field equations that the infinitesimal differential element approach enables the transition to, from discrete free-body diagrams, for analyzing rod deformation behavior.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e2db8e0cc453f4ff50201dc37d1fa0c</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thermal Elongation Equation">
  <data key="d0">Thermal Elongation Equation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The equation Δl₁⁽⁰⁾ = u_c⁽⁰⁾ = α_T · ΔT · l representing the thermal elongation of a single bar (Einzelstab) in a statically determinate reference system (state 0), used within a superposition method for solving statically indeterminate problems</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-542bf3a4290d267cd5257b52563c594f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Linear Thermal Strain Relationship">
  <data key="d0">Linear Thermal Strain Relationship</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The classical relationship ε_T = α_T · ΔT, which when integrated over the bar length yields Δl = α_T · ΔT · l, representing pure thermal deformation</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-542bf3a4290d267cd5257b52563c594f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Statically Determinate Base System">
  <data key="d0">Statically Determinate Base System</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The reference system (state 0) representing the unconstrained or released system used as the first sub-problem in the superposition approach</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-542bf3a4290d267cd5257b52563c594f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Doubly Clamped Statically Indeterminate Bar System">
  <data key="d0">Doubly Clamped Statically Indeterminate Bar System</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A bar system clamped on both sides (beidseitig eingespannt) creating static indeterminacy that requires the superposition method for thermoelastic analysis</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-542bf3a4290d267cd5257b52563c594f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pipelines">
  <data key="d0">Pipelines</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Constrained structures in which thermal stresses are analyzed using the superposition approach in structural mechanics&lt;SEP&gt;Engineering structures where the vessel formula is applied for stress prediction and failure prevention in design</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-542bf3a4290d267cd5257b52563c594f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-493acae899ca4eaaedf536afa97f481b</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903997</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Railway Tracks">
  <data key="d0">Railway Tracks</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Constrained structures in which thermal stresses are analyzed using the superposition approach in structural mechanics</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-542bf3a4290d267cd5257b52563c594f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Composite Structural Elements">
  <data key="d0">Composite Structural Elements</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Constrained structures in which thermal stresses are analyzed using the superposition approach in structural mechanics</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-542bf3a4290d267cd5257b52563c594f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mechanical Normal Force">
  <data key="d0">Mechanical Normal Force</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Also known as Normalkraft, a mechanical force that is absent in the pure thermal deformation represented by state 0 of the superposition method</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-542bf3a4290d267cd5257b52563c594f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Δl₁⁽⁰⁾">
  <data key="d0">Δl₁⁽⁰⁾</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The length change of bar 1 in the statically determinate base system (state 0) due to pure thermal expansion</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-542bf3a4290d267cd5257b52563c594f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="u_c⁽⁰⁾">
  <data key="d0">u_c⁽⁰⁾</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The displacement at point C in the unconstrained system during pure thermal expansion, which must be compensated by a corrective displacement u_c⁽¹⁾</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-542bf3a4290d267cd5257b52563c594f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="u_c⁽¹⁾">
  <data key="d0">u_c⁽¹⁾</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The corrective displacement at point C resulting from an imposed reaction force, which compensates for the thermal expansion u_c⁽⁰⁾</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-542bf3a4290d267cd5257b52563c594f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Boundary Condition Δl = Δl₁ + Δl₂ = 0">
  <data key="d0">Boundary Condition Δl = Δl₁ + Δl₂ = 0</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The constraint in the doubly clamped system requiring that the total displacement at the fixed support C vanishes</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-542bf3a4290d267cd5257b52563c594f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Statically Indeterminate Thermoelastic Problem">
  <data key="d0">Statically Indeterminate Thermoelastic Problem</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A structural mechanics problem involving thermal effects in a constrained system, which is transformed by the superposition approach into two solvable sub-problems</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-542bf3a4290d267cd5257b52563c594f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reaction Force">
  <data key="d0">Reaction Force</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The compressive reaction force (Normalkraft), denoted as F_x, that develops at the supports of the clamped compound rod due to thermal loading.&lt;SEP&gt;An imposed mechanical force that generates the corrective displacement u_c⁽¹⁾ to enforce compatibility in the constrained system</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-542bf3a4290d267cd5257b52563c594f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c71f393772a794391e49730d47a8bda4</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ε_T">
  <data key="d0">ε_T</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The classical linear thermal strain, defined as the product of the coefficient of thermal expansion and the temperature change</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-542bf3a4290d267cd5257b52563c594f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Equilibrium Equation N + dN + n.dx - N = 0">
  <data key="d0">Equilibrium Equation N + dN + n.dx - N = 0</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A mathematical equation summing forces in the axial direction to zero for static equilibrium of a differential element.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f862d3f8b712d95184fc656859d1e6cd</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infinitesimal Equilibrium Condition">
  <data key="d0">Infinitesimal Equilibrium Condition</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Also known as Gleichgewichtsbedingung, it is the static equilibrium condition for a one-dimensional bar element under axial loading.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f862d3f8b712d95184fc656859d1e6cd</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="One-Dimensional Bar Element">
  <data key="d0">One-Dimensional Bar Element</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A structural element, referred to as Einzelstab, analyzed under axial loading.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f862d3f8b712d95184fc656859d1e6cd</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Differential Element">
  <data key="d0">Differential Element</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An infinitesimal segment of length extracted from a bar for analyzing internal forces.&lt;SEP&gt;A light-gray filled square representing a differential element of a material body, oriented at a tilt at the center of the technical schematic diagram.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f862d3f8b712d95184fc656859d1e6cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-153ac624cdef095260ab75841c027b8f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904048</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Differential Increment Of Axial Force">
  <data key="d0">Differential Increment Of Axial Force</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The value dN, representing the change in axial force on the right face of the element at position x+dx.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f862d3f8b712d95184fc656859d1e6cd</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infinitesimal Length">
  <data key="d0">Infinitesimal Length</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The length, denoted as dx, of the extracted differential element.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f862d3f8b712d95184fc656859d1e6cd</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Constitutive/Elasticity Laws">
  <data key="d0">Constitutive/Elasticity Laws</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">One of the three fundamental equation types needed to solve bar problems, describing material behavior.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f862d3f8b712d95184fc656859d1e6cd</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Differential Form dN/dx = -n">
  <data key="d0">Differential Form dN/dx = -n</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The simplified differential equation derived by dividing the algebraically simplified equilibrium equation by dx.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f862d3f8b712d95184fc656859d1e6cd</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Kinematic Relation ε = du/dx">
  <data key="d0">Kinematic Relation ε = du/dx</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The strain-displacement relation combined with the differential form to derive the governing equation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f862d3f8b712d95184fc656859d1e6cd</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hooke's Law σ = E·ε">
  <data key="d0">Hooke's Law σ = E·ε</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The elasticity law combined with the differential form to derive the bar's deformation equation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f862d3f8b712d95184fc656859d1e6cd</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Newton's First Law">
  <data key="d0">Newton's First Law</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The physical principle expressed by the infinitesimal equilibrium condition for a continuum element.&lt;SEP&gt;Physical law enforcing static equilibrium, applied in the tangential direction by setting the sum of forces equal to zero.&lt;SEP&gt;Physical principle applied to a differential element to derive equilibrium conditions</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f862d3f8b712d95184fc656859d1e6cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e48d7926a99342f43a9d78825059455&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20d2489764cb6b004e3ff06ba7ebe0c1</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904035</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Continuum Element">
  <data key="d0">Continuum Element</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A continuous differential material element for which Newton's first law is physically expressed by the equilibrium condition.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f862d3f8b712d95184fc656859d1e6cd</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="u_c^(1)">
  <data key="d0">u_c^(1)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Displacement at point C in the correction state (1) of the superposition method.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5e6428916bed03d77d29954942400a6f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="State 0">
  <data key="d0">State 0</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A statically determinate system state representing unconstrained thermal expansion.&lt;SEP&gt;A free-expansion case used in the principle of superposition to decompose the thermal loading problem.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5e6428916bed03d77d29954942400a6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed4c24e6b357be46b6c720d32cdb5f62</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="State 1">
  <data key="d0">State 1</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A statically determinate system state loaded by the redundant constraint force F_x.&lt;SEP&gt;A force-correcting case used in the principle of superposition to satisfy boundary conditions after free expansion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5e6428916bed03d77d29954942400a6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed4c24e6b357be46b6c720d32cdb5f62</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Axial Length Change Delta l_1">
  <data key="d0">Axial Length Change Delta l_1</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The axial length change of rod segment 1 in state (1).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5e6428916bed03d77d29954942400a6f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Axial Length Change Delta l_2">
  <data key="d0">Axial Length Change Delta l_2</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The axial length change of rod segment 2 in state (1).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5e6428916bed03d77d29954942400a6f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Horizontal Constraint Force F_x">
  <data key="d0">Horizontal Constraint Force F_x</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A horizontal constraint force (Lagerreaktion) acting at point C.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5e6428916bed03d77d29954942400a6f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rod Segment Length l">
  <data key="d0">Rod Segment Length l</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The common length of both rod segments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5e6428916bed03d77d29954942400a6f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hooke's Law For Axial Deformation">
  <data key="d0">Hooke's Law For Axial Deformation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A physical law stating axial deformation is proportional to applied force, formulated as Delta l = Nl/EA.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5e6428916bed03d77d29954942400a6f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Doubly-clamped Rod">
  <data key="d0">Doubly-clamped Rod</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A beidseitig eingespannter Stab subjected to thermal loading.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5e6428916bed03d77d29954942400a6f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rod Segment 1">
  <data key="d0">Rod Segment 1</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The first physical segment of the analyzed rod.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5e6428916bed03d77d29954942400a6f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rod Segment 2">
  <data key="d0">Rod Segment 2</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The second physical segment of the analyzed rod.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5e6428916bed03d77d29954942400a6f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="u_c^(0)">
  <data key="d0">u_c^(0)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Displacement at point C in state (0) of the superposition method.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5e6428916bed03d77d29954942400a6f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Spring Networks">
  <data key="d0">Spring Networks</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A system whose mathematical structure is mirrored by the serial arrangement of compliances in the rod.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5e6428916bed03d77d29954942400a6f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Composite Material Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Composite Material Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An analysis field that shares the mathematical structure of series compliance addition.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5e6428916bed03d77d29954942400a6f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Linear Elastic Systems">
  <data key="d0">Linear Elastic Systems</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Systems whose superposition is a fundamental concept demonstrated by the formulation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5e6428916bed03d77d29954942400a6f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Applied End Force">
  <data key="d0">Applied End Force</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Represented by F, the force applied at the end of the bar. When n = 0, the normal force N equals this applied end force as a constant throughout the bar.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-413d03b5c0b6ff01a4da279c609d09f9</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deformation">
  <data key="d0">Deformation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The change in shape or size of axially-loaded structural members, determined using the mathematical foundation established by the equilibrium equation and finite element formulation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-413d03b5c0b6ff01a4da279c609d09f9</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Kinematic Compatibility Equation">
  <data key="d0">Kinematic Compatibility Equation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A mathematical equation representing the kinematic compatibility condition for a statically indeterminate, two-sided clamped compound rod subjected to thermal loading.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c71f393772a794391e49730d47a8bda4</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Compound Rod">
  <data key="d0">Compound Rod</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A statically indeterminate, two-sided clamped rod composed of two segments with different cross-sectional areas but equal length.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c71f393772a794391e49730d47a8bda4</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thermal Expansion Coefficient">
  <data key="d0">Thermal Expansion Coefficient</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The coefficient of linear thermal expansion (Wärmeausdehnungskoeffizient), denoted as alpha_T, which determines the free thermal expansion of a rod segment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c71f393772a794391e49730d47a8bda4</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rod Segment">
  <data key="d0">Rod Segment</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A section of the compound rod, specifically segment 1 and segment 2, which have different cross-sectional areas but equal length.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c71f393772a794391e49730d47a8bda4</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="F1 = F2 + n·l">
  <data key="d0">F1 = F2 + n·l</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Mathematical equation representing the axial force equilibrium condition (Gleichgewichtsbedingung) for a single bar element subjected to point forces and distributed line loads, stating that the normal force at one end equals the normal force at the other end plus the resultant of the distributed load over the segment length</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-faaf238bf3e3a6116edca46159e939df</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="F1">
  <data key="d0">F1</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Internal normal force (Normalkraft) at one endpoint of a bar segment, denoting the axial force at the first end of the element</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-faaf238bf3e3a6116edca46159e939df</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="F2">
  <data key="d0">F2</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Internal normal force (Normalkraft) at the other endpoint of a bar segment, denoting the axial force at the second end of the element</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-faaf238bf3e3a6116edca46159e939df</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Normal Force Diagrams">
  <data key="d0">Normal Force Diagrams</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Diagrams (N-Verläufe) showing the distribution of normal force along a bar's longitudinal axis, constructed using the axial force equilibrium relationship</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-faaf238bf3e3a6116edca46159e939df</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Trusses">
  <data key="d0">Trusses</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Structural systems composed of axially loaded members, where the axial force equilibrium equation is foundational for analysis</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-faaf238bf3e3a6116edca46159e939df</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Uniform Loading">
  <data key="d0">Uniform Loading</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A special case of distributed loading where n is constant along the bar length, allowing the integral of distributed load to simplify to n·l</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-faaf238bf3e3a6116edca46159e939df</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Support Reaction Force Equation">
  <data key="d0">Support Reaction Force Equation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">An equation calculating the support reaction forces for a statically indeterminate, doubly-clamped rod with two segments of different cross-sectional areas under uniform thermal loading.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ed4c24e6b357be46b6c720d32cdb5f62</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Doubly-Clamped Rod">
  <data key="d0">Doubly-Clamped Rod</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A statically indeterminate structural member consisting of two segments with different cross-sectional areas, fixed at both ends, subject to constrained thermal expansion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ed4c24e6b357be46b6c720d32cdb5f62</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="F_x">
  <data key="d0">F_x</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The compressive normal force induced in the rod due to constrained thermal expansion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ed4c24e6b357be46b6c720d32cdb5f62</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Support Reaction Force B">
  <data key="d0">Support Reaction Force B</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The support reaction force at the left clamp of the doubly-clamped rod.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ed4c24e6b357be46b6c720d32cdb5f62</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Support Reaction Force C">
  <data key="d0">Support Reaction Force C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The support reaction force at the right clamp of the doubly-clamped rod.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ed4c24e6b357be46b6c720d32cdb5f62</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Effective Axial Stiffness">
  <data key="d0">Effective Axial Stiffness</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The term EA1A2/(A1+A2), representing the axial stiffness of the two-segment bar in series, analogous to the harmonic mean of the individual stiffnesses scaled by E.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ed4c24e6b357be46b6c720d32cdb5f62</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Longitudinal Strain Field">
  <data key="d0">Longitudinal Strain Field</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The local relative deformation (elongation or contraction per unit length) at a given position, represented as ε(x), acting as a kinematic quantity independent of material properties.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-635877c2ca4bd8652a8de3e6ef23d5f9</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lagrangian Coordinate">
  <data key="d0">Lagrangian Coordinate</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The material coordinate (x) along a rod's longitudinal axis, measured in the undeformed reference configuration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-635877c2ca4bd8652a8de3e6ef23d5f9</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Strain-displacement Relation">
  <data key="d0">Strain-displacement Relation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A fundamental geometric compatibility relationship in solid mechanics defining strain as the first-order spatial derivative of axial displacement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-635877c2ca4bd8652a8de3e6ef23d5f9</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Small-strain Assumption">
  <data key="d0">Small-strain Assumption</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A linearized kinematics assumption under which the strain-displacement relation is derived.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-635877c2ca4bd8652a8de3e6ef23d5f9</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thermal Strain Term">
  <data key="d0">Thermal Strain Term</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An additional strain component (ε_th = α·ΔT) introduced by temperature effects, which modifies the constitutive relation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-635877c2ca4bd8652a8de3e6ef23d5f9</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Finite Element Stiffness Matrices">
  <data key="d0">Finite Element Stiffness Matrices</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Matrices formulated for truss and bar elements, relying on the strain-displacement relation to analyze structural systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-635877c2ca4bd8652a8de3e6ef23d5f9</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Derivative Operator">
  <data key="d0">Derivative Operator</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The ordinary (total) derivative operator (d/dx) used in the equation, assuming a one-dimensional, uniaxial state of deformation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-635877c2ca4bd8652a8de3e6ef23d5f9</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Equilibrium Equation">
  <data key="d0">Equilibrium Equation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A mathematical expression (dN/dx + n = 0) that relates the derivative of the internal normal force to external distributed loads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-635877c2ca4bd8652a8de3e6ef23d5f9</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Second-order Governing Differential Equation">
  <data key="d0">Second-order Governing Differential Equation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A differential equation for the displacement field (d/dx[EA·du/dx] + n = 0) derived by combining kinematic, constitutive, and equilibrium relations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-635877c2ca4bd8652a8de3e6ef23d5f9</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Temperature Effects">
  <data key="d0">Temperature Effects</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Thermal variations (ΔT) that introduce an additional thermal strain term, thereby modifying the material's constitutive relation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-635877c2ca4bd8652a8de3e6ef23d5f9</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Direct Solution">
  <data key="d0">Direct Solution</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">An approach to solving statically indeterminate systems using equilibrium conditions, kinematic relationships, and boundary conditions where total elongation is zero.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2866a3f417ff78b075338fa558392e29</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="0-system">
  <data key="d0">0-system</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A statically determinate subsystem in the superposition principle characterized by pure thermal expansion and the absence of normal force.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2866a3f417ff78b075338fa558392e29</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="1-system">
  <data key="d0">1-system</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A subsystem in the superposition principle that is loaded with constraint forces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2866a3f417ff78b075338fa558392e29</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Both-sides Clamped Rod">
