</node>
<node id="Tangent Function">
  <data key="d0">Tangent Function</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A trigonometric function noted as being periodic, used in the analysis of extreme values of stresses.&lt;SEP&gt;A trigonometric function with a period of π used to determine principal stress directions, yielding two angles separated by π/2 (90 degrees).&lt;SEP&gt;A mathematical function whose periodicity leads to two perpendicular cutting directions (principal directions) where extreme stress values occur.&lt;SEP&gt;A mathematical function whose periodicity produces two perpendicular principal directions when solving tan(2φ*) = 2τ_xy/(σ_x−σ_y).&lt;SEP&gt;A periodic mathematical function used in the formula to yield the two perpendicular section directions for extremal normal stresses.&lt;SEP&gt;A trigonometric function periodic with period π, whose periodicity yields two orthogonal solutions for principal angles</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ba92f82e2b057ed886fb58574a01ea0a-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da8ea347d2fe041d08bb85c59209fc9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85ca1064506b38c8fe493e3ffc533c71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e8a589d6ecd831cc0e1afc0b83e4bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-788996859590fcaca4ffb066d7148714&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2839b8d3cca96c984fc98ff0599ca3a1</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904035</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
