  <data key="d1">equation</data>
  <data key="d2">An equation displaying fractional tuples (2/5, 3/5) likely representing normalized trigonometric or stress components used in computing principal stresses (Hauptspannungen) and principal directions (Hauptrichtungen). The notation appears non-standard, possibly denoting the ratio tan(2φ*) = 2τxy/(σx−σy) within Section 11.2.2 of the stress transformation framework, where shear stresses vanish at extremal normal stress values.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0fca9235e4f945947ddf250020a6f05e</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784901716</data>
