<node id="Principal Stress Direction Equation (tan 2φ*) (equation)">
  <data key="d0">Principal Stress Direction Equation (tan 2φ*) (equation)</data>
  <data key="d1">equation</data>
  <data key="d2">This equation identifies the principal angle φ* at which normal stresses reach extremal values (principal stresses σ₁ and σ₂) and shear stresses vanish. It forms the mathematical foundation for coordinate transformation in plane stress analysis, connecting the general stress state (σ_x, σ_y, τ_xy) to the principal stress directions in continuum mechanics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-788996859590fcaca4ffb066d7148714</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784901716</data>
