<node id="Diagram of Principal Stress State and Orientation (image)">
  <data key="d0">Diagram of Principal Stress State and Orientation (image)</data>
  <data key="d1">image</data>
  <data key="d2">This diagram illustrates the principal stress state (Hauptspannungen) of a material element as described in Section 11.2.2. It shows a square element rotated by an angle $\\varphi^*$ into the principal coordinate system (axes 1 and 2). In this orientation, shear stresses are zero, and the normal stresses acting perpendicular to the faces are at their extreme values, labeled as the principal stresses $\\sigma_1$ and $\\sigma_2$. The visual clearly distinguishes between the principal axes (blue), the stress vectors (red), and the principal angle (green).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a8be23ae96862171a1f9cb78cb1cfcb0</data>
