  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Invalid Equation">
  <data key="d0">Invalid Equation</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The equation (0)(0 - 1/2) × (0.25 - 0.5) = 1.5 which is mathematically invalid, as the left-hand side evaluates to zero, not 1.5. Possibly a transcription error, placeholder, or malformed expression.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a5f08150d01a4afad6a7e20e54169ec1</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mohr's Circle Center">
  <data key="d0">Mohr's Circle Center</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The center of Mohr's circle, calculated using the formula sigma_M = (sigma_x + sigma_y)/2, representing the average of the normal stress components.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a5f08150d01a4afad6a7e20e54169ec1</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mohr's Circle Radius">
  <data key="d0">Mohr's Circle Radius</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The radius of Mohr's circle, calculated as R = sqrt(((sigma_x - sigma_y)/2)^2 + tau_xy^2), used to determine the magnitude of principal stresses.&lt;SEP&gt;The radius R of Mohr's Circle, determined using the Euclidean norm of stress differences: R = sqrt(((σ_x - σ_y)/2)^2 + τ_xy^2).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a5f08150d01a4afad6a7e20e54169ec1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bcd5ad0575ad16303ca4601a26ea32f2</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Normal Stress Transformation">
  <data key="d0">Normal Stress Transformation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The stress transformation equation sigma(varphi) = sigma_M + R*cos(2*varphi) for calculating normal stress at a given rotation angle varphi.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a5f08150d01a4afad6a7e20e54169ec1</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Shear Stress Transformation">
  <data key="d0">Shear Stress Transformation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The stress transformation equation tau(varphi) = R*sin(2*varphi) for calculating shear stress at a given rotation angle varphi.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a5f08150d01a4afad6a7e20e54169ec1</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sigma-Tau Plane">
  <data key="d0">Sigma-Tau Plane</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The coordinate plane (sigma, tau) in which Mohr's stress circle is geometrically constructed using known stress components sigma_x, sigma_y, and tau_xy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a5f08150d01a4afad6a7e20e54169ec1</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stress Transformation Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Stress Transformation Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The broader analytical framework within which Mohr's stress circle is used to perform stress transformations, involving rotating coordinate systems by angle varphi.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a5f08150d01a4afad6a7e20e54169ec1</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rotation Angle Varphi">
  <data key="d0">Rotation Angle Varphi</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The angle of rotation between the x,y and the xi,eta coordinate systems used in stress transformation.&lt;SEP&gt;The angle varphi by which coordinate systems are rotated during stress transformation, with 2*varphi represented on Mohr's circle.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a5f08150d01a4afad6a7e20e54169ec1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f852bec3a8e229cf7fc9b647545ae29</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="2D State Of Stress Diagram">
  <data key="d0">2D State Of Stress Diagram</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A technical schematic diagram illustrating a two-dimensional state of stress at a point within a material, showing a differential element with stress components as red vector arrows within a Cartesian coordinate system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e57c82a12143d5b7fd3e7f96dc75f203</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Differential Material Element">
  <data key="d0">Differential Material Element</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
