<node id="Trigonometric Identities">
  <data key="d0">Trigonometric Identities</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Trigonometric identities are mathematical equations and relations that are extensively utilized in the field of mechanics, particularly for deriving and simplifying stress transformation equations during coordinate rotations. By applying these mathematical relations, complex stress equations can be systematically reduced into standard, manageable formulas used to calculate shear and normal stresses. 

In the context of stress transformations, specific algebraic and angle-based trigonometric identities are substituted into derivations to simplify the equations. For instance, angle-shift identities such as cos(phi + pi/2) = -sin(phi) are used to simplify equations into the standard formula for normal stresses, such as Sigma Eta. Additionally, fundamental power-reduction and double-angle identities—namely cos²φ = (1+cos2φ)/2, sin²φ = (1-cos2φ)/2, and 2sinφcosφ = sin2φ—are applied to derive the standard double-angle forms of the stress transformation equations.

Furthermore, trigonometric identities involving sin(2φ*) and cos(2φ*) are integral to the subsequent derivation steps needed to obtain explicit expressions for principal stresses, specifically σ_1 and σ_2. These identities allow for sin(2φ*) and cos(2φ*) to be expressed as rational functions of the base stress components. By translating these trigonometric terms into rational functions, the identities provide a comprehensive mathematical bridge to accurately derive principal stresses directly from standard normal and shear stress components.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd1f71b01c1aa5c67c36a16a597748fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-792f1aab7b01df3f4ae8fa499208a41a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3780797c1d45f39538f2b68c98e007f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fca9235e4f945947ddf250020a6f05e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6643a9ec6dd9b81db5b4233bf1899ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20d2489764cb6b004e3ff06ba7ebe0c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf5a136f98019f0bd369d2b6d44879f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a03cb4a8bcb2904e74a15376b18fddec</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903867</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Point P">
  <data key="d0">Point P</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A specific spatial location in a deformable body at which the stress state is evaluated, requiring specification across all possible cutting planes for complete description.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific point identified within the cross-section A of the solid body.&lt;SEP&gt;A reference point marked by an open circle at the rear-bottom-left corner of the volume element, serving as the origin of local coordinates for stress analysis&lt;SEP&gt;A reference point through which coordinate axes pass, used for deriving moment equilibrium conditions that establish shear stress symmetry.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific point within a deformable body where the stress state is characterized.&lt;SEP&gt;A point located in the upper-right quadrant of Mohr's Circle with coordinates (σ_x, τ_xy), connected by a vertical line to σ_x on the horizontal axis.&lt;SEP&gt;A point on Mohr's Circle at coordinates representing the stress state on the x-face.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-842c0517bb20a54922d1a75c277c68f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-341774a38a3b4fd47c6656391af81dd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c2c59e0f6a23f968e67f68fc9498278&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7876e6fbf1af5b17253567ec9af4cf91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cabab253ce4ee75c98c51cfd7f1a27b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d97fb385691a70a5c314b2a77a107e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13b9a52b59b74e8f8b6c3180f71ccba2</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903867</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Point P'">
  <data key="d0">Point P'</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A point located in the lower-left quadrant of Mohr's Circle with coordinates (σ_y, -τ_xy), connected by a vertical line to σ_y on the horizontal axis.&lt;SEP&gt;A point on Mohr's Circle representing the stress state on the perpendicular y-face.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-842c0517bb20a54922d1a75c277c68f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-341774a38a3b4fd47c6656391af81dd6</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
