</node>
<node id="σ_M">
  <data key="d0">σ_M</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The symbol representing normal stresses acting perpendicularly outward from each face of the material element, specifically denoting the mean normal stress or the normal stress value at the orientation of maximum shear.&lt;SEP&gt;The center point of Mohr's Circle on the horizontal σ-axis, calculated as σ_M = 1/2(σ_x + σ_y).&lt;SEP&gt;The center of the Mohr's Circle lying on the σ-axis midway between the two principal stress intersection points, representing the mean normal stress.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-842c0517bb20a54922d1a75c277c68f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30b2a42c115ed62e72e715daa89e2370&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-012dfb2f1f77750672c0c98cb5c5f782</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903867</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="τ">
  <data key="d0">τ</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Greek letter tau representing shear stress, labeled on the vertical axis of the coordinate system used in Mohr's Circle.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-842c0517bb20a54922d1a75c277c68f0</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
