<node id="Radius">
  <data key="d0">Radius</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The distance from the center to the edge of Mohr's Circle, denoted by $r$.&lt;SEP&gt;A line segment labeled '$r$' extending from the center $\sigma_M$ to point P.&lt;SEP&gt;A geometric property of the Mohr's Circle that corresponds to the value of the maximum shear stress (τ_max).&lt;SEP&gt;The radius of Mohr's stress circle ($R$), calculated from the stress state components to be approximately 46.1 MPa&lt;SEP&gt;The radius $r$ of the thin-walled cylindrical pressure vessel.&lt;SEP&gt;Denoted as r, it represents the radius of the spherical shell of the thin-walled pressure vessel.&lt;SEP&gt;The geometric distance from the center to the edge of the spherical vessel, denoted by 'r'.</data>
