<node id="σ_x">
  <data key="d0">σ_x</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The entity σ_x represents the normal stress acting along the x-axis, specifically defined as the normal stress on the face perpendicular to the x-axis. It is fundamentally characterized as the normal stress in the original x-direction within an (x, y)-coordinate system, serving as a primary normal stress component of the original coordinate system and the two-dimensional stress tensor.

As a critical variable in engineering mechanics, σ_x is utilized as an input component in several fundamental mathematical formulations, including the normal stress transformation formula and the principal stress equation. Furthermore, in the graphical method of stress analysis known as Mohr's Circle, σ_x represents the x-coordinate of Point P, which is plotted on the horizontal σ-axis. 

In specific loading conditions, such as a state of uniaxial tension, σ_x constitutes the only non-zero normal stress present, making it equivalent to the first principal stress, σ_1. In practical application, such as in the worked example problem found on page 26, σ_x is assigned a value of 50 MPa to serve as a quantitative input parameter for calculating stress transformation equations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-842c0517bb20a54922d1a75c277c68f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb966affea49c8515afe80d893d4ba39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c03dbd78277681c5ab7e7802efbca7b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e8a589d6ecd831cc0e1afc0b83e4bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-788996859590fcaca4ffb066d7148714&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9d228101e892c4b9b284f5228fa25ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f2990ab5263ad174ce6fec37fef1115&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b5475536a7fccb42b9f6f9e39d32b77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1f8906173d951132fd77877e8868d53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20d2489764cb6b004e3ff06ba7ebe0c1</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
