<node id="τ_xy">
  <data key="d0">τ_xy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">τ_xy is a shear stress variable that represents the shear stress acting on the xy-plane within an original (x, y)-coordinate system. It serves as a fundamental input parameter in several mechanics of materials equations. Specifically, τ_xy is utilized in the principal stress equation and appears in the normal stress transformation formula, where it constitutes a part of the deviatoric contribution. 

In the graphical analysis of stress, τ_xy holds specific geometric significance within Mohr's Circle. It represents the y-coordinate of Point P, while simultaneously corresponding to the negative of the y-coordinate for Point P' on the circle. 

Beyond its theoretical definitions, τ_xy is frequently applied as an initial value in practical stress transformation problems. For example, in a specific worked example problem located on page 26, the original shear stress τ_xy is assigned a value of 30 MPa. When processed through the stress transformation equation, the magnitude of this original input parameter (τ_xy) is shown to be larger than the resulting transformed shear stress component, τ_{ξη}.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-842c0517bb20a54922d1a75c277c68f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb966affea49c8515afe80d893d4ba39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e8a589d6ecd831cc0e1afc0b83e4bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-788996859590fcaca4ffb066d7148714&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9d228101e892c4b9b284f5228fa25ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f2990ab5263ad174ce6fec37fef1115&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b5475536a7fccb42b9f6f9e39d32b77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1f8906173d951132fd77877e8868d53</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903913</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
