<node id="Mohr's Circle">
  <data key="d0">Mohr's Circle</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Mohr's Circle, also known as Mohrscher Spannungskreis, is a foundational graphical and analytical method used in continuum mechanics, engineering mechanics, and materials science. It serves as a comprehensive visual framework for analyzing the state of stress at a specific point within a material. By mapping the state of stress as a locus of points in a Cartesian coordinate system, it provides a geometric alternative to algebraic stress transformation equations, effectively simplifying the notation for normal and shear stresses.

The construction of Mohr's Circle is fundamentally based on the theory of principal stresses and the stress transformation law, specifically deriving from the symmetric 2D Cauchy stress tensor. In its standard graphical representation, normal stress (σ) is plotted on the horizontal axis, and shear stress (τ) is plotted on the vertical axis. The center of the circle is located on the horizontal σ-axis at the mean stress point (σ_M). A defining characteristic of this method is that angular relationships on the circle are doubled relative to physical space, incorporating double-angle transformation terms such as cos(2φ*) and sin(2φ*).

Mohr's Circle is primarily utilized to perform coordinate transformations and determine critical stress values. It enables the precise determination of principal stresses—which are found at the intersection points of the circle and the σ-axis—and maximum shear stresses, along with their corresponding physical orientations. The framework systematically analyzes various stress states, including the two-dimensional plane stress state. It is commonly used to illustrate and evaluate special cases such as uniaxial tension, pure shear stress (which serves as part of its physical basis), and the hydrostatic stress state. In the specific case of hydrostatic stress, the circle's radius becomes zero, causing it to degenerate into a single point.

Beyond theoretical stress transformation, Mohr's Circle serves as a vital technical diagram in practical structural mechanics. It is employed to evaluate stress states in complex engineering scenarios, such as pressure vessel analysis, and to determine normal and shear stresses on arbitrary inclined sections. Additionally, it is used to predict the yielding and failure of materials subjected to complex, multi-axial loading conditions, making it an indispensable tool in the design and analysis of structures and mechanical components.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-842c0517bb20a54922d1a75c277c68f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6513413e0a80f005888472d94d385e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-792f1aab7b01df3f4ae8fa499208a41a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb966affea49c8515afe80d893d4ba39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-341774a38a3b4fd47c6656391af81dd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b44241248f288278ba7f5d8fa8160e3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85ca1064506b38c8fe493e3ffc533c71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e48d7926a99342f43a9d78825059455&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30b2a42c115ed62e72e715daa89e2370&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98f7f241f746726b97e3dc567365e483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e8a589d6ecd831cc0e1afc0b83e4bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3780797c1d45f39538f2b68c98e007f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c2c59e0f6a23f968e67f68fc9498278&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95ef86ae323cfba68764c2acb2d46785&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97ae2381cfa6e993a16166b7495765c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74378ee7045b50cecf2c625c47685477&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fca9235e4f945947ddf250020a6f05e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6ea2012f708d083bcf1f8357bfab292&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40562a8ce19d10e78736b201626c9b32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05f0cba91a41b2018384acbb7174e398&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9d228101e892c4b9b284f5228fa25ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2662124ebaa998fdaa13ffecb3add380&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebe13321a6d5df3c82e760adc093a99c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d8ef0753f64ed72eb451c29b8108d08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-153ac624cdef095260ab75841c027b8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82d26e50b1a6b9a189224f9805e4217e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae7aec8cf21235bd79c851b9cc6978f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb9e40b1a13627933f97ce043e59f768&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3553477d678ccfb56c56a99c6a713a1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6643a9ec6dd9b81db5b4233bf1899ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34f056013d274101fd8fe012cf408b4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cae0fdb4f5af9a553af5e5ec7a633b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f56ba60dee95d9f5127479d5f80c141c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ca440e5727deb504109d3cda9b3642d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95309ae773a0c5fe9703868d35942eff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1f8906173d951132fd77877e8868d53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b47aa4fc45ad067947c357da574f854&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4df6ac3e36adc464a8f9e47b557ec07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20d2489764cb6b004e3ff06ba7ebe0c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b625d3948531b3dcd9b53a158a3a5265&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f29928f565c2e69c