<node id="Thin-walled Vessel Theory">
  <data key="d0">Thin-walled Vessel Theory</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A theoretical framework studied under internal and external pressure loading conditions, sourced from Technische Mechanik 2.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f61ee301f89076e345159fdaef391ab6</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903914</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="σ_y">
  <data key="d0">σ_y</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">σ_y represents the normal stress component acting in the original y-direction within an (x,y)-coordinate system. In the context of a two-dimensional stress tensor or an infinitesimal quader, it is defined as the normal stress acting on the faces perpendicular to the y-axis. Physically, this stress component acts horizontally on the y-faces (left and right) of the element, pointing rightward on the positive y-face and leftward on the negative y-face.

As a fundamental variable in mechanics, σ_y is utilized in various stress analysis equations and graphical methods. It serves as an essential input component in both the normal stress transformation formula and the principal stress equation. Additionally, when analyzing stresses graphically using Mohr's Circle, σ_y represents the x-coordinate of Point P' located on the horizontal σ-axis.

In practical applications, such as the worked example problem on page 26, σ_y is assigned a specific value of -20 MPa. This negative value denotes a compressive stress acting in the y-direction, which is subsequently applied as a direct input parameter in the stress transformation equations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-842c0517bb20a54922d1a75c277c68f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb966affea49c8515afe80d893d4ba39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c03dbd78277681c5ab7e7802efbca7b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e8a589d6ecd831cc0e1afc0b83e4bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-788996859590fcaca4ffb066d7148714&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9d228101e892c4b9b284f5228fa25ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f2990ab5263ad174ce6fec37fef1115&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b5475536a7fccb42b9f6f9e39d32b77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1f8906173d951132fd77877e8868d53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20d2489764cb6b004e3ff06ba7ebe0c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23912fb95dffaea41a466afd896e511</data>
