<node id="Tensor Invariants">
  <data key="d0">Tensor Invariants</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Properties of the stress tensor that remain unchanged under coordinate rotation, including the trace and determinant.&lt;SEP&gt;An engineering mechanics concept related to tensor properties, discussed in the document.&lt;SEP&gt;Quantities such as (σ_x + σ_y) that remain unchanged under coordinate rotation&lt;SEP&gt;Quantities that remain unchanged under coordinate transformation, including the sum σ_x + σ_y and the determinant σ_x·σ_y - τ_xy².&lt;SEP&gt;Properties of the stress tensor that remain constant regardless of coordinate system rotation, including the trace equal to the sum of principal stresses.&lt;SEP&gt;Invariants of the 2D Cauchy stress tensor related to the principal stress and eigenvalue problem framework.</data>
