</node>
<node id="Biaxial Stress State">
  <data key="d0">Biaxial Stress State</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A stress state in which stresses act in two perpendicular directions, governing the design of thin-walled pressure vessels.&lt;SEP&gt;A uniform stress state in the thin-walled spherical pressure vessel resulting from tangential stress being equal to circumferential stress.&lt;SEP&gt;The state of stress within a spherical vessel under internal pressure, which the diagram visualizes.&lt;SEP&gt;A stress state distributing load in two perpendicular directions, reflected by the factor 1/2 in the spherical vessel formula, contrasting with the cylindrical case where hoop stress carries twice the load of longitudinal stress.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb31546e781f11ba51b9575be2e9cb66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73adfabedf760785acfd7b799786f369&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1f8906173d951132fd77877e8868d53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bd1d5444d931cb0efa80cdff770977</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903947</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Spherical Vessel">
  <data key="d0">Spherical Vessel</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of thin-walled pressure vessel where both tangential stresses are equal: σ_t = σ_φ = p·r/(2t).&lt;SEP&gt;A vessel subjected to internal pressure, within which a biaxial stress state occurs.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of pressure vessel under internal pressure with an equibiaxial stress state where σ_t = σ_φ</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb31546e781f11ba51b9575be2e9cb66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-493acae899ca4eaaedf536afa97f481b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9c3492ddaae5a544709ab9626c48a75</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903947</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Meridional Stress">
  <data key="d0">Meridional Stress</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of stress synonymous with tangential stress, represented by the vertical pair of arrows and the Greek symbol sigma subscript t.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb31546e781f11ba51b9575be2e9cb66</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903947</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hoop Stress">
  <data key="d0">Hoop Stress</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The circumferential stress (sigma_phi) in a pressure vessel wall, which according to boiler formulas is twice the longitudinal stress.&lt;SEP&gt;The circumferential stress (Umfangsspannung) in a cylindrical vessel, denoted σ_φ = p·r/t, representing one of the principal stresses in thin-walled vessel analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of stress synonymous with circumferential stress, represented by the horizontal pair of arrows and the Greek symbol sigma subscript phi.&lt;SEP&gt;The circumferential stress (Umfangsspannungen, σ_φ) experienced by the walls of a pressure vessel.&lt;SEP&gt;The circumferential stress σ_φ acting in the vessel wall, measured in Pascals [Pa], producing a resultant force σ_φ · 2πrt over the cross-sectional annular area.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb31546e781f11ba51b9575be2e9cb66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73adfabedf760785acfd7b799786f369&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e80e31b80a7c1439506d701b5bbac342&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b625d3948531b3dcd9b53a158a3a5265&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9c3492ddaae5a544709ab9626c48a75</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903947</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
