<node id="Provenance Tracking">
  <data key="d0">Provenance Tracking</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The practice of tracking the origins and ownership of documents, data, or academic content to ensure proper attribution and authenticity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5db8101dd80f03fc824342c78093902c</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903967</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Normal Stress Transformation Equation">
  <data key="d0">Normal Stress Transformation Equation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The transformation rule for the normal stress component in a two-dimensional plane stress state under a rotation of the coordinate system, calculating the normal stress acting on a plane whose normal vector is rotated by an angle relative to the original x-axis.&lt;SEP&gt;Represents the coordinate transformation for the normal stress component σ_η in a two-dimensional stress state under rotation of the reference frame by angle φ. It decomposes the transformed normal stress into three contributions: the mean stress, a deviatoric normal stress term, and a shear stress contribution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eb966affea49c8515afe80d893d4ba39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f852bec3a8e229cf7fc9b647545ae29</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903967</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="σ_η">
  <data key="d0">σ_η</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A stress component calculated through a π/2 rotation of σ_ξ, introduced on page 13 of the German mechanics document.&lt;SEP&gt;Normal stress in the rotated η-direction, calculated by the Normal Stress Transformation Equation.&lt;SEP&gt;Normal stress in the rotated η-direction of the (ξ,η)-coordinate system, obtained by rotating the original (x,y)-axes by angle φ.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eb966affea49c8515afe80d893d4ba39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e8a589d6ecd831cc0e1afc0b83e4bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b5475536a7fccb42b9f6f9e39d32b77</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903967</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="φ">
  <data key="d0">φ</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Rotation angle from the x,y-coordinate system to the ξ,η-system.&lt;SEP&gt;Rotation angle of the coordinate system used in the stress transformation equations.&lt;SEP&gt;Rotation angle used to transform from the original (x,y)-coordinate system to the rotated (ξ,η)-coordinate system in plane stress analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eb966affea49c8515afe80d893d4ba39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e8a589d6ecd831cc0e1afc0b83e4bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20d2489764cb6b004e3ff06ba7ebe0c1</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903967</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mean Stress">
  <data key="d0">Mean Stress</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A stress quantity mathematically formulated as ΔF/ΔA approaching a limit.&lt;SEP&gt;Calculated as (1/2)(σ_x + σ_y), represents the hydrostatic component and is an invariant of the stress tensor.&lt;SEP&gt;The average of the principal stresses, denoted by $\sigma_m$, evaluated using 45-degree trigonometric identities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eb966affea49c8515afe80d893d4ba39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eadc704f7f5e7980d43e7d870873727e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f29928f565c2e69cfd84b7a3af24ffe</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903969</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deviatoric Normal Stress Term">
  <data key="d0">Deviatoric Normal Stress Term</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Term involving (σ_x - σ_y)cos(2φ), one of three contributions to the transformed normal stress in the transformation equation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eb966affea49c8515afe80d893d4ba39</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903969</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Shear Stress Transformation Equation">
  <data key="d0">Shear Stress Transformation Equation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The equation τ_ξη = -(σ_x - σ_y)sin(φ)cos(φ) + τ_xy(cos²φ - sin²φ) representing the shear stress transformation relation for a plane stress state under rotation of the coordinate system by an angle φ, which can be rewritten in canonical form as τ_ξη = -½(σ_x - σ_y)sin(2φ) + τ_xy·cos(2φ).&lt;SEP&gt;τ_ξη = (1/2)(σ_x - σ_y)sin(2φ) + τ_xy cos(2φ), the corresponding equation describing how shear stress transforms under coordinate rotation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eb966affea49c8515afe80d893d4ba39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d77ac531ca72db1dfb705ad40ac98c3f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903969</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="τ_ξη">
  <data key="d0">τ_ξη</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Shear stress in the rotated coordinate system, calculated by the Shear Stress Transformation Equation.&lt;SEP&gt;Shear stress in the ξη-plane of the rotated (ξ,η)-coordinate system, related to the derivative of σ_ξ by dσ_ξ/dφ = 2τ_ξη.&lt;SEP&gt;The shear stress in the principal directions, which theoretically vanishes.&lt;SEP&gt;The shear stress on the principal planes that vanishes identically at the principal angle φ = φ*.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eb966affea49c8515afe80d893d4ba39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e8a589d6ecd831cc0e1afc0b83e4bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-788996859590fcaca4ffb066d7148714&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9d228101e892c4b9b284f5228fa25ad</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903969</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Trace Of Stress Tensor">
  <data key="d0">Trace Of Stress Tensor</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The quantity σ_x + σ_y, which remains invariant across all coordinate systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eb966affea49c8515afe80d893d4ba39</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903969</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vector Transformations">
  <data key="d0">Vector Transformations</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Mathematical transformations for vectors that do not use a factor of 2 in trigonometric arguments, distinguishing them from second-rank tensor transformations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eb966affea49c8515afe80d893d4ba39</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903969</data>
