<node id="Optical Character Recognition">
  <data key="d0">Optical Character Recognition</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A technology whose severe corruption produced the provided equation, which was originally a transformation equation for a 2D plane stress state.&lt;SEP&gt;A technology (OCR) whose error or parsing artifact likely produced the nonsensical equation presented in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;A technology whose failure in interpreting subscripts like sigma_1 and sigma_2 likely resulted in the corrupted constants in the provided equation.&lt;SEP&gt;A text recognition technology that caused severe errors and corruptions in the provided mathematical equation.&lt;SEP&gt;A digitization technique that likely caused corruption in the provided LaTeX equation, introducing recurring artifacts like 'nuptermation'.&lt;SEP&gt;A technology that converts images of text into machine-encoded text, which misidentified Greek sigma as bold theta and misinterpreted fractions and subscripts in the equation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68094852a469c1054fde9d0f452e6077&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da8ea347d2fe041d08bb85c59209fc9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b47aa4fc45ad067947c357da574f854&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f29928f565c2e69cfd84b7a3af24ffe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bcd5ad0575ad16303ca4601a26ea32f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aecddc3be14bd893c4f22755acfb1f21</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903990</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="2D Plane Stress State">
  <data key="d0">2D Plane Stress State</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Also known as 'ebener Spannungszustand', this is the physical scenario the original intended expression describes before OCR corruption.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68094852a469c1054fde9d0f452e6077</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903990</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rotation Angle">
  <data key="d0">Rotation Angle</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Denoted as $\varphi$, this is the angle used in trigonometric functions within the transformation equation for the stress state.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68094852a469c1054fde9d0f452e6077</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903990</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Double-angle Trigonometric Identities">
  <data key="d0">Double-angle Trigonometric Identities</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Mathematical identities used to derive the transformation equation for the stress state, along with power-reduction identities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68094852a469c1054fde9d0f452e6077</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903990</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zero-product Property">
  <data key="d0">Zero-product Property</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A mathematical principle stating that if any multiplicand in a product is zero, the entire product evaluates to zero.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68094852a469c1054fde9d0f452e6077</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903990</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Trace">
  <data key="d0">Trace</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A tensor invariant of the stress tensor calculated as ($\sigma_x + \sigma_y$), representing the sum of normal stresses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68094852a469c1054fde9d0f452e6077</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903990</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Maximum Shear Stresses">
  <data key="d0">Maximum Shear Stresses</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The highest shear stresses experienced by a material at a given point, determined using stress transformation and Mohr's circle.&lt;SEP&gt;The highest shear stress values and their corresponding orientations determined graphically using Mohr's circle.&lt;SEP&gt;Maximum values of shear stress determined through stress transformation, critical for predicting material failure&lt;SEP&gt;Specific stress values determined using coordinate transformations, representing the largest shear stress at a point.&lt;SEP&gt;The maximum shear stress values at a point, determined through Mohr's circle construction as part of practical engineering stress analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68094852a469c1054fde9d0f452e6077&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae7aec8cf21235bd79c851b9cc6978f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34f056013d274101fd8fe012cf408b4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b625d3948531b3dcd9b53a158a3a5265&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf5a136f98019f0bd369d2b6d44879f8</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903990</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Materials Engineering">
  <data key="d0">Materials Engineering</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A field in which coordinate transformation of stress states is applied for failure analysis of structural components.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68094852a469c1054fde9d0f452e6077</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903990</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
