</node>
<node id="Externally Pressurized Vessels">
  <data key="d0">Externally Pressurized Vessels</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of vessel to which the vessel formulas (Kesselformeln) are applicable; in these vessels, the pressure sign changes resulting in compressive stresses.&lt;SEP&gt;Vessels subjected to external pressure, for which the vessel formula applies by changing the sign, resulting in compressive stresses</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-493acae899ca4eaaedf536afa97f481b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd415d5735a4c089d6c4d66fc2f63d48</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903997</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Compressive Stresses">
  <data key="d0">Compressive Stresses</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Stresses that occur in externally pressurized vessels due to a change in the pressure sign.&lt;SEP&gt;Stresses resulting from the application of the vessel formula to externally pressurized vessels, where the sign is reversed compared to internal pressure&lt;SEP&gt;Stresses resulting from external pressure, obtained by reversing the sign of p in the equilibrium equation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-493acae899ca4eaaedf536afa97f481b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73adfabedf760785acfd7b799786f369&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd415d5735a4c089d6c4d66fc2f63d48</data>
