<node id="φ*">
  <data key="d0">φ*</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The critical or principal angle at which the normal stress reaches its maximum or minimum value, and at which the shear stress τ_ξη vanishes identically.&lt;SEP&gt;The principal angle identifying the principal directions.&lt;SEP&gt;A critical section orientation relevant to the relationship between normal stresses and shear stresses discussed in the document.&lt;SEP&gt;The angle defining the principal directions in the stress transformation.&lt;SEP&gt;The principal stress orientation angle from which the orientation of maximum shear stress (φ**) is offset by π/4 radians.</data>
