<node id="Angle φ">
  <data key="d0">Angle φ</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The angle characterizing the rotation from the x,y-coordinate system to the rotated η,ξ-system during coordinate transformation of stress components.&lt;SEP&gt;The angle marked in green that defines the rotation between the Cartesian and rotated coordinate systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The angle by which the x,y-coordinate system is rotated to the ξ,η-coordinate system.&lt;SEP&gt;The physical rotation angle of the stress element, defining an arbitrary plane, represented as twice its value (2φ) in the diagram.&lt;SEP&gt;The angle of 30° formed by the normal of the sectional plane with the original x-axis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae7aec8cf21235bd79c851b9cc6978f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c2cf3a337f73c88af5880c2708e9c48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ca440e5727deb504109d3cda9b3642d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1f8906173d951132fd77877e8868d53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b3409eb9a461816c78110bf52f37f07</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904048</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
