<node id="Infinitesimal Triangular Element">
  <data key="d0">Infinitesimal Triangular Element</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A small geometric shape used as a analytical tool on page 12 for the derivation of stress components under rotated coordinate systems.&lt;SEP&gt;An abstract geometric element used for equilibrium considerations during coordinate transformations.&lt;SEP&gt;An element first introduced on page 11, used as the basis for equilibrium considerations in the derivation of stress components under coordinate system rotation.&lt;SEP&gt;A small triangular element extracted from a thin plate under plane stress, used to analyze equilibrium conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;A differential geometric element cut from a two-dimensional stress element (Scheibe) used to analyze force equilibrium on an inclined surface.&lt;SEP&gt;A small triangular element cut from a thin plate (Scheibe), used to derive the stress transformation equations from equilibrium conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a2f298ccb33e1f76a031a29e81e1f9dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34f056013d274101fd8fe012cf408b4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b5475536a7fccb42b9f6f9e39d32b77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87396546f57986339f19784a816ba8db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20d2489764cb6b004e3ff06ba7ebe0c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d77ac531ca72db1dfb705ad40ac98c3f</data>
