</node>
<node id="Panel D">
  <data key="d0">Panel D</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A longitudinal section of a cylinder segment of length Δl, showing internal pressure p acting vertically on the projected area (2r · Δl) and the resulting circumferential stress σφ acting upwards along the cut edges of the wall thickness t, fundamental for deriving the relationship between internal pressure and hoop stress through vertical force equilibrium.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7b026fcfc3bb4dcf15d90b692b7902eb</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904052</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Surface Element">
  <data key="d0">Surface Element</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A small, light-green square element highlighted on the outer surface of the cylinder in panel a, representing an infinitesimal material point used for local stress analysis of the biaxial stress state.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7b026fcfc3bb4dcf15d90b692b7902eb</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904052</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cylinder Segment Length">
  <data key="d0">Cylinder Segment Length</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The length denoted as Δl, representing the length of the cylinder segment shown in the longitudinal section view in panel d.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7b026fcfc3bb4dcf15d90b692b7902eb</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904052</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vertical Force Equilibrium">
  <data key="d0">Vertical Force Equilibrium</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The method of establishing vertical force equilibrium in panel d, used to derive the relationship between internal pressure and circumferential (hoop) stress.&lt;SEP&gt;A mechanical principle used on page 29 for the derivation of circumferential/hoop stresses (Umfangsspannungen σφ) in a thin-walled vessel.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7b026fcfc3bb4dcf15d90b692b7902eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd415d5735a4c089d6c4d66fc2f63d48</data>
