<edge source="Normal Stress" target="Cauchy's Stress Principle">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The normal stress equation is derived from Cauchy's stress principle for a uniaxially loaded structural member.</data>
  <data key="d9">derived from,fundamental definition</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-61bee0456fb356f553c6809b0f9fb7ef</data>
  <data key="d11">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1784897128</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Normal Stress" target="External Axial Load">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Normal stress is defined as the external axial load divided by the cross-sectional area, expressed as σ = F/A.</data>
  <data key="d9">defined by,ratio</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-61bee0456fb356f553c6809b0f9fb7ef</data>
  <data key="d11">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1784897128</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Normal Stress" target="Uniform Stress Distribution">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The normal stress equation embodies the assumption of uniform stress distribution across the cross-section.</data>
  <data key="d9">assumes,basis</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-61bee0456fb356f553c6809b0f9fb7ef</data>
  <data key="d11">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1784897128</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Normal Stress" target="Strength of Materials">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The normal stress relationship is foundational in strength of materials (Festigkeitslehre), serving as the basis for more complex stress analyses.</data>
  <data key="d9">basis,foundational</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-61bee0456fb356f553c6809b0f9fb7ef</data>
  <data key="d11">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1784897128</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Normal Stress" target="Elasticity Theory">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The normal stress relationship is foundational in elasticity theory (Elastizitätsmodell).</data>
  <data key="d9">basis,foundational</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-61bee0456fb356f553c6809b0f9fb7ef</data>
  <data key="d11">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1784897128</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Normal Stress" target="Hooke's Law">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The normal stress equation connects to kinematic relationships through Hooke's Law and strain calculations.</data>
  <data key="d9">connects through,relationship</data>
