</edge>
<edge source="r(x)" target="r_0">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The geometric function r(x) uses the initial radius r_0 to calculate the local radius.</data>
  <data key="d9">parameterized by,uses</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-1b5a4dfb0ae1aefebcb3a9f19f155c76</data>
  <data key="d11">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1784897127</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="r(x)" target="l">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The geometric function r(x) uses the total length l as a scaling factor.</data>
  <data key="d9">parameterized by,uses</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-1b5a4dfb0ae1aefebcb3a9f19f155c76</data>
  <data key="d11">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1784897127</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="r(x)" target="x">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">r(x) is a continuous, monotonically increasing linear function of the axial position x.</data>
  <data key="d9">depends on,function of</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-1b5a4dfb0ae1aefebcb3a9f19f155c76</data>
  <data key="d11">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1784897127</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="l" target="n">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The distributed line load n is computed as n = G/l, where l is the bar length.</data>
  <data key="d9">derived from,equals</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-b5cc011b4f71d9c304cbdecd2839b81e</data>
  <data key="d11">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1784897128</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="l" target="Einzelstab">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The total length of the Einzelstab is indicated by the variable l.</data>
  <data key="d9">dimension,length</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-17b87724a453e2805522671a76c088ec</data>
  <data key="d11">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1784897129</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="l" target="Δl = α_T · ΔT · l">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">l is the original length of the bar used in the thermal expansion equation</data>
  <data key="d9">contains,uses</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-370a72fe18982a27d4543ffa0c4c20f0</data>
  <data key="d11">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1784897130</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="l" target="G">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The total weight G of the rod is proportional to its length l, as G = ρgAl.</data>
  <data key="d9">proportional to</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-213cdd3f8f32396583dc5a4fa4d54dfd</data>
  <data key="d11">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1784897130</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="l" target="Bar Element">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">l is the length of the bar segment over which forces and distributed loads act</data>
  <data key="d9">geometric parameter,property of</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-faaf238bf3e3a6116edca46159e939df</data>
  <data key="d11">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1784897132</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="x" target="Differential Segment">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The variable x indicates the distance from the left origin to the left boundary of the green differential segment.</data>
  <data key="d9">measures distance to</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-ba3dc6bb30208edf4354dd20376fa9f6</data>
  <data key="d11">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1784897129</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="x" target="N(x)">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The internal normal force N(x) decreases linearly from G at the support (x=0) to zero at the free end (x=l).</data>
  <data key="d9">decreases linearly,varies with</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-213cdd3f8f32396583dc5a4fa4d54dfd</data>
  <data key="d11">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1784897130</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="x" target="σ(x)">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The axial stress σ(x) varies linearly with position x, being maximum (G/A) at x=0 and zero at x=l.</data>
  <data key="d9">linear,varies with</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-213cdd3f8f32396583dc5a4fa4d54dfd</data>
  <data key="d11">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1784897130</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A(x)" target="σ(x)">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The normal stress distribution σ(x) is calculated by dividing the internal force N(x) by the cross-sectional area A(x).</data>
  <data key="d9">computed from,depends on</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-1b5a4dfb0ae1aefebcb3a9f19f155c76</data>
  <data key="d11">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1784897127</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="σ(x)" target="N(x)">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The normal stress distribution σ(x) depends on the constant compressive internal force N(x).&lt;SEP&gt;The axial stress σ(x) is defined as the ratio of internal normal force N(x) to cross-sectional area A (σ = N(x)/A).</data>
  <data key="d9">computed from,depends on,ratio of</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-1b5a4dfb0ae1aefebcb3a9f19f155c76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-213cdd3f8f32396583dc5a4fa4d54dfd</data>
  <data key="d11">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1784897127</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="σ(x)" target="Axial Stress Distribution Equation">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The equation defines the axial stress distribution σ(x) = N(x)/A = (G/A)(1 - x/l) along the hanging rod.</data>
  <data key="d9">defines,describes</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-213cdd3f8f32396583dc5a4fa4d54dfd</data>
  <data key="d11">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1784897130</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="N(x)" target="Equation dN/dx + n = 0">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The equation describes the differential equilibrium condition in which the spatial gradient of the normal force N(x) must exactly balance the applied distributed load.</data>
  <data key="d9">describes,involves</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-b5cc011b4f71d9c304cbdecd2839b81e</data>
  <data key="d11">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1784897128</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="N(x)" target="Stress Definition">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The stress definition involves the internal normal force N(x).</data>
  <data key="d9">involves,uses</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-b5cc011b4f71d9c304cbdecd2839b81e</data>
  <data key="d11">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1784897128</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
