  <data key="d10">chunk-c97b092fc202625d8ee8acd1894cf787</data>
  <data key="d11">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1784897128</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Governing ODE For Axial Displacement" target="Hanging Bar Under Self-Weight">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The governing ODE is applied to the hanging bar under self-weight, a statically determinate problem.</data>
  <data key="d9">applied to</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-c97b092fc202625d8ee8acd1894cf787</data>
  <data key="d11">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1784897128</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Governing ODE For Axial Displacement" target="Single Rod">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The governing second-order ordinary differential equation describes the axial displacement of a single rod or bar.</data>
  <data key="d9">applied to</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-c97b092fc202625d8ee8acd1894cf787</data>
  <data key="d11">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1784897128</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Governing ODE For Axial Displacement" target="Kinematic Relation">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The governing ODE is derived by combining the kinematic relation ε = u'(x) with the equilibrium condition and Hooke's law</data>
  <data key="d9">derived_from</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-f4f759f99f5a784630c625df026ca993</data>
