  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Axial Displacement Field" target="Derivative Operator">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The derivative operator is applied to the axial displacement field to calculate the local gradient, provided the field is at least once differentiable.</data>
  <data key="d9">application,differentiation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-635877c2ca4bd8652a8de3e6ef23d5f9</data>
  <data key="d11">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1784897132</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Axial Displacement Field" target="Axial Strain">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Axial strain is defined as the first derivative of the axial displacement field with respect to position.</data>
