  <data key="d12">1784897129</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Governing Ordinary Differential Equation (ODE)" target="One-dimensional Equilibrium Condition">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The governing ODE is mathematically derived by combining the one-dimensional equilibrium condition with the constitutive law.</data>
  <data key="d9">arises from,derived from</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-1dfca5c7dbae86836330061b0f49bc01</data>
  <data key="d11">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1784897129</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Governing Ordinary Differential Equation (ODE)" target="Linear-elastic Constitutive Law">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The governing ODE is formed by incorporating the linear-elastic constitutive law into the equilibrium condition.</data>
  <data key="d9">arises from,derived from</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-1dfca5c7dbae86836330061b0f49bc01</data>
  <data key="d11">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1784897129</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Governing Ordinary Differential Equation (ODE)" target="General Solution u(x)">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The general solution is found by integrating the governing ODE twice to determine the axial displacement field.</data>
  <data key="d9">integrates,solves</data>
