  <data key="d11">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1784904222</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hydrostatic Stress State" target="Sonderfall 3">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The hydrostatic stress state is designated as Sonderfall 3 in the Mohr's Circle analysis framework.</data>
  <data key="d9">categorization,designation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-0d8ef0753f64ed72eb451c29b8108d08</data>
  <data key="d11">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1784904224</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hydrostatic Stress State" target="Mohr's Circle">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Under the hydrostatic stress state, Mohr's circle degenerates to a single point at (σ_0, 0) with a radius of zero.</data>
  <data key="d9">degeneration,geometric interpretation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-0d8ef0753f64ed72eb451c29b8108d08</data>
  <data key="d11">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1784904224</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hydrostatic Stress State" target="Deviatoric Stress Decomposition">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The hydrostatic stress state acts as the volumetric component that separates from the distortional component during deviatoric stress decomposition.</data>
  <data key="d9">component,separation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-0d8ef0753f64ed72eb451c29b8108d08</data>
  <data key="d11">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1784904224</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hydrostatic Stress State" target="Sonderfall 1">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Unlike uniaxial tension (Sonderfall 1), the hydrostatic stress state produces no distortion.</data>
  <data key="d9">comparison,contrast</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-0d8ef0753f64ed72eb451c29b8108d08</data>
  <data key="d11">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1784904224</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hydrostatic Stress State" target="Sonderfall 2">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Unlike pure shear (Sonderfall 2), the hydrostatic stress state produces no distortion.</data>
  <data key="d9">comparison,contrast</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-0d8ef0753f64ed72eb451c29b8108d08</data>
  <data key="d11">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1784904224</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hydrostatic Stress State" target="Principal Stresses">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">In the hydrostatic stress state, the principal stresses are degenerate with σ_1 = σ_2 = σ_0, making every direction a principal direction.</data>
  <data key="d9">degenerate,mathematical property</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-0d8ef0753f64ed72eb451c29b8108d08</data>
  <data key="d11">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1784904224</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hydrostatic Stress State" target="Maximum Shear Stress">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The maximum shear stress equals zero in the hydrostatic stress state regardless of orientation.</data>
  <data key="d9">physical property,zero</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-0d8ef0753f64ed72eb451c29b8108d08</data>
  <data key="d11">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1784904225</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hydrostatic Stress State" target="Stress Invariants">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The hydrostatic stress state connects to the concept of stress invariants because the stress tensor is rotationally invariant.</data>
  <data key="d9">connected concept,mathematical property</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-0d8ef0753f64ed72eb451c29b8108d08</data>
  <data key="d11">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1784904225</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
