<edge source="Principal Stresses" target="Mohr's Circle">
  <data key="d7">10.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation between Mohr's Circle and Principal Stresses encompasses the use of Mohr's Circle as a graphical framework and analytical basis for determining principal stresses in structural engineering. Primarily, Mohr's Circle acts as a graphical representation that enables the calculation and expression of principal stresses using simplified notation. Its construction is fundamentally based on the underlying theory of principal stresses.

Through this method, principal stresses can be effectively determined from a given biaxial stress state. Specifically, the exact values of the principal stresses are located at the points where the Mohr's Circle intersects the horizontal axis, commonly referred to as the σ-axis. These intersections serve as the definitive geometric mechanism for identifying and calculating the principal stresses within the analyzed system.</data>
  <data key="d9">based on,basis,calculation,computes,determination,determines,framework,graphical method,identifies,intersection points,intersects,represents,stress transformation,visualization</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-341774a38a3b4fd47c6656391af81dd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c2c59e0f6a23f968e67f68fc9498278&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fca9235e4f945947ddf250020a6f05e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae7aec8cf21235bd79c851b9cc6978f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb9e40b1a13627933f97ce043e59f768&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6643a9ec6dd9b81db5b4233bf1899ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ca440e5727deb504109d3cda9b3642d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b47aa4fc45ad067947c357da574f854&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b625d3948531b3dcd9b53a158a3a5265&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf5a136f98019f0bd369d2b6d44879f8</data>
  <data key="d11">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1784904198</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
