<edge source="Hoop Stress" target="Longitudinal Stress">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">According to boiler formulas, hoop stress is twice the longitudinal stress in a thin-walled pressure vessel.&lt;SEP&gt;In a cylindrical vessel, hoop stress is twice the longitudinal stress: σ_φ = 2·σ_x.&lt;SEP&gt;For cylindrical vessels under internal pressure, hoop stress is exactly twice the longitudinal stress (σ_φ = 2·σ_x).&lt;SEP&gt;In a cylindrical case, the longitudinal stress carries half the load compared to the hoop stress.</data>
  <data key="d9">compared to,load ratio,proportional to,ratio,stress relationship</data>
